(PREFACE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Designed mainly for class room use in connection with one of the) Tj T*
(introductory manuals on the subject of Money and Banking or of Money and) Tj T*
(Currency, this volume, _in itself_, lays no claim to completeness. Where) Tj T*
(its use is contemplated the problems of emphasis and proportion are,) Tj T*
(accordingly, to be solved by the selection of one or another of the) Tj T*
(available texts, or by the choice of supplementary lecture topics and) Tj T*
(materials. The contents of the introductory manuals are so divergent in) Tj T*
(character as to render possible combinations of text and readings that) Tj T*
(will include, it is hoped, matter of such range and variety as may be) Tj T*
(desired.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Fullness of treatment has been attempted, however, in the chapters) Tj T*
(dealing with the important recent developments in the "mechanism of) Tj T*
(exchange," and my aim has been throughout to select and, in many) Tj T*
(instances, to adapt with a view to meeting the wants of those who are) Tj T*
(interested chiefly in the modern phases of the subject.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For valuable suggestions in the preparation of the volume I am greatly) Tj T*
(indebted to Professors F. H. Dixon and G. R. Wicker and Mr. J. M.) Tj T*
(Shortliffe of Dartmouth, Professor Hastings Lyon of Columbia, Professor) Tj T*
(E. E. Day of Harvard, and to my former teacher, Professor F. R.) Tj T*
(Fairchild of Yale. I desire also to mention my great obligation to) Tj T*
(authors and publishers who alike have generously permitted the) Tj T*
(reproduction of copyrighted material.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
