(CHAPTER I) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE ORIGIN AND FUNCTIONS OF MONEY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([1]In order to understand the manifold functions of a Circulating) Tj T*
(Medium, there is no better way than to consider what are the principal) Tj T*
(inconveniences which we should experience if we had not such a medium.) Tj T*
(The first and most obvious would be the want of a common measure for) Tj T*
(values of different sorts. If a tailor had only coats, and wanted to buy) Tj T*
(bread or a horse, it would be very troublesome to ascertain how much) Tj T*
(bread he ought to obtain for a coat, or how many coats he should give) Tj T*
(for a horse. The calculation must be recommenced on different data,) Tj T*
ET
