(THE EFFECTS OF GREENBACKS UPON WAGES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Statistical evidence supports unequivocally the common theory that) Tj T*
(persons whose incomes are derived from wages suffer seriously from a) Tj T*
(depreciation of the currency. The confirmation seems particularly) Tj T*
(striking when the conditions other than monetary affecting the labour) Tj T*
(market are taken into consideration. American workingmen are intelligent) Tj T*
(and keenly alive to their interests. There are probably few districts) Tj T*
(where custom plays a smaller and competition a larger role in) Tj T*
(determining wages than in the Northern States. While labor organisations) Tj T*
(had not yet attained their present power, manual laborers did not fail) Tj T*
(to avail themselves of the help of concerted action in the attempt to) Tj T*
(secure more pay. Strikes were frequent. All these facts favored a speedy) Tj T*
(readjustment of money wages to correspond with changed prices. But more) Tj T*
(than all else, a very considerable part of the labor supply was) Tj T*
(withdrawn from the market into the army and navy. In 1864 and 1865 about) Tj T*
(one million of men seem to have been enrolled. About one-seventh of the) Tj T*
(labor supply withdrew from the market. But despite all these favoring) Tj T*
(circumstances, the men who stayed at home did not succeed in obtaining) Tj T*
(an advance in pay at all commensurate with the increase in living) Tj T*
