(unstable currency is generally held to make business unsafe, and seldom) Tj T*
(has the standard money of a mercantile community proven so unstable,) Tj T*
(undergone such violent fluctuations in so short a time, as in the United) Tj T*
(States during the Civil War. Yet, instead of being extremely hazardous,) Tj T*
(business seems from the statistics of failures to have been more than) Tj T*
(usually safe.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The explanation of the anomaly seems to be that the very extremity of) Tj T*
(the danger proved a safeguard. Business men realized that the inflation) Tj T*
(of prices was due to the depreciation of the currency, and that when the) Tj T*
(war was over gold would fall and prices follow. They realized very) Tj T*
(clearly the necessity of taking precautions against being caught in a) Tj T*
(position where a sudden decline of prices would ruin them. They did this) Tj T*
(by curtailing credits. So long as prices continued to rise such) Tj T*
(precautions were really not needed by the man in active business except,) Tj T*
(in so far as he was a creditor of other men; but when prices commenced) Tj T*
(to fall prudence had its reward. Such a sudden and violent drop of) Tj T*
(prices as occurred between January and July, 1865, would have brought a) Tj T*
(financial revulsion of a most serious character upon a business) Tj T*
(community under ordinary circumstances. But so well had the change been) Tj T*
(prepared for, that the number of failures was actually less than it had) Tj T*
(been in the preceding year of rapidly rising prices.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
