(What influence did the greenback currency have as one of the many) Tj T*
(factors that affected the production of wealth? In the first place, the) Tj T*
(paper standard was responsible in large measure for the feeling of) Tj T*
("prosperity" that seems from all the evidence to have characterized the) Tj T*
(public's frame of mind. Almost every owner of property found that the) Tj T*
(price of his possessions had increased, and almost every wage-earner) Tj T*
(found that his pay was advanced. Strive as people may to emancipate) Tj T*
(themselves from the feeling that a dollar represents a fixed quantity of) Tj T*
(desirable things, it is very difficult for them to resist a pleasurable) Tj T*
(sensation when the money value of their property rises or their incomes) Tj T*
(increase. They are almost certain to feel cheerful over the larger sums) Tj T*
(that they can spend, even though the amount of commodities the larger) Tj T*
(sums will buy is decreased. Habit is too strong for arithmetic.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
