(unusually profitable during the war. The "residual claimant" is in most) Tj T*
(enterprises the active business man, and, as has been shown, his money) Tj T*
(income did as a rule rise more rapidly than the cost of living. In other) Tj T*
(words, "business" was, in reality as well as in appearance, rendered) Tj T*
(more profitable by the greenbacks. There is therefore no error in saying) Tj T*
(that the business of the country enjoyed unwonted prosperity during the) Tj T*
(war. And it may be added that the active business man is probably a more) Tj T*
(potent factor in determining the community's feeling about "good times") Tj T*
(and "bad times" than is the workingman, the landlord, or the lending) Tj T*
(capitalist.) Tj T*
