(CONTRACTION AND INFLATION OF THE LEGAL TENDERS[9]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The policy of a permanent currency of government legal-tender paper at) Tj T*
(the close of the Civil War was unknown. Upwards of four hundred million) Tj T*
(notes of the United States were, it is true, in circulation at the) Tj T*
(return of peace. There were doubtless many individuals who approved the) Tj T*
(continuance of exactly this form of currency. But no such proposition) Tj T*
(had been advanced by any public man of influence or by any political) Tj T*
(organization. That the resort to legal-tender powers was an evil) Tj T*
(justified only by extreme emergency, and that the circulation of) Tj T*
(government notes in any form was a purely temporary measure, were the) Tj T*
(unanimous convictions of the statesmen who contrived the system. The) Tj T*
(logical inference that these Government notes would be paid off and) Tj T*
(cancelled, as soon as the war deficiency had ended, was publicly) Tj T*
(accepted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Such was the theory and purpose of the public men through whom the) Tj T*
(Legal-Tender Act was constructed and applied. Nor is the general) Tj T*
(position of our statesmen, at the close of the Civil War, any more) Tj T*
(obscure than their original position. The first financial resolution) Tj T*
(adopted by Congress, in December, 1865, was an explicit promise to) Tj T*
(retire the legal tenders. The first legislation of that Congress gave) Tj T*
(discretionary powers to the Secretary of the Treasury for continuous) Tj T*
(contraction. Very few legislative victories are won without at least a) Tj T*
(temporary popular endorsement, and the votes of December, 1865, and of) Tj T*
(March, 1866, were no exceptions. But the popular approval of contraction) Tj T*
(in that year, exception as it was to all our subsequent legislation, is) Tj T*
(readily enough explained. Public opinion, when the war ended, was) Tj T*
(governed by impatience with inflated prices; inflation far beyond the) Tj T*
(European level, and properly ascribed to the condition of the currency.) Tj T*
