(1878 provided for the purchase by the Government, each month, of not) Tj T*
(less than two million dollars' worth, and not more than four million) Tj T*
(dollars' worth of silver bullion, for coinage into silver dollars at the) Tj T*
(rate of 412-1/2 grains of standard silver \(or 371-1/4 grains of fine) Tj T*
(silver\) for each dollar. The amount of the purchases, within the) Tj T*
(specified limits, was left to the discretion of the Secretary of the) Tj T*
(Treasury. As every Secretary of the Treasury, throughout the period in) Tj T*
(which the act was in force, kept to the minimum amount, the practical) Tj T*
(result was a monthly purchase of two million dollars' worth of silver) Tj T*
(bullion.) Tj T*
