(States became gold, and the extent of the coinage of silver dollars) Tj T*
(under the act of 1878 became simply a question of how much silver) Tj T*
(bullion could be bought with two million dollars of gold. The price of) Tj T*
(silver in 1878 was, in terms of gold, not far from a dollar for an ounce) Tj T*
(of standard silver. Since 1878 it has gone down almost steadily, and ...) Tj T*
