(the best-known index numbers, that of the _Economist_, is thus) Tj T*
(constructed. Twenty-two articles having been selected, the price of each) Tj T*
(article at the current date compared with its price at the standard) Tj T*
(period \(1845-50\) is expressed as a percentage; and the sum of these) Tj T*
(percentages is put as the index number. Thus the _Economist_ index) Tj T*
(number for the year 1873 is 2947; such a sum is easily reduced to the) Tj T*
(form of an average by simple division \(_e. g._, 2947 / 22 = 134\).) Tj T*
