(IRVING FISHER[43]: Overlooking the influence of deposit currency, or) Tj T*
(checks, the price level may be said to depend on only three sets of) Tj T*
(causes: \(1\) the quantity of money in circulation; \(2\) its "efficiency") Tj T*
(or velocity of circulation \(or the average number of times a year money) Tj T*
(is exchanged for goods\); and \(3\) the volume of trade \(or amount of goods) Tj T*
(bought by money\). The so-called "quantity theory,"[44] _i.e._, that) Tj T*
(prices vary proportionately to money, has often been incorrectly) Tj T*
(formulated, but \(overlooking checks\) the theory is correct in the sense) Tj T*
(that the level of prices varies directly with the quantity of money in) Tj T*
(circulation, provided the velocity of circulation of that money and the) Tj T*
(volume of trade which it is obliged to perform are not changed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The quantity theory has been one of the most bitterly contested theories) Tj T*
(in economics, largely because the recognition of its truth or falsity) Tj T*
(affected powerful interests in commerce and politics. It has been) Tj T*
(maintained--and the assertion is scarcely an exaggeration--that the) Tj T*
(theorems of Euclid would be bitterly controverted if financial or) Tj T*
(political interests were involved.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The quantity theory has, unfortunately, been made the basis of arguments) Tj T*
(for unsound currency schemes. It has been invoked in behalf of) Tj T*
(irredeemable paper money and of national free coinage of silver at the) Tj T*
(ratio of 16 to 1. As a consequence, not a few "sound money men,") Tj T*
