(THE GOLD EXCHANGE STANDARD) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     It is an essential feature of the gold exchange standard as) Tj T*
(     it exists in the Philippines, for example, that premiums) Tj T*
(     charged by the Government in Manila for exchange on New) Tj T*
(     York, and in New York for exchange on Manila are fixed at a) Tj T*
(     point somewhat below the gold export points in each case.) Tj T*
(     Thus the would-be exporter of gold in the Philippines never) Tj T*
(     finds it profitable to ship gold to New York. On the other) Tj T*
(     hand, international bankers in New York never find it) Tj T*
(     profitable to ship gold or currency to the Philippines,) Tj T*
(     because the authorised agent of the Philippine government in) Tj T*
(     New York always stands ready to sell in exchange for United) Tj T*
(     States currency, drafts drawn upon Manila at a premium less) Tj T*
(     than the cost of shipping gold or currency. Through a) Tj T*
(     regulation of the supply of silver pesos in actual) Tj T*
(     circulation in the Philippines they are maintained at a) Tj T*
(     definite ratio to--not gold in the Philippines, but--gold,) Tj T*
(     or its equivalent, in New York. The way in which the supply) Tj T*
(     of local currency in the gold-exchange country is regulated) Tj T*
(     will be made clear in what follows.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     The gold exchange standard has not entirely escaped) Tj T*
(     criticism. Professor J. Shield Nicholson has recently) Tj T*
(     attacked this standard in India. \(_Economic Journal_, June,) Tj T*
(     1914.\) It is his contention that inflation may occur in) Tj T*
(     India, if it has not already occurred, on account of the) Tj T*
(     "impeded convertibility of rupees into gold." After a) Tj T*
(     certain point is reached in the inflation the decline in the) Tj T*
(     general purchasing power of the rupee must be followed, he) Tj T*
(     affirms, by a specific depreciation as regards gold; and) Tj T*
(     then the main object of the plan would be defeated. He) Tj T*
(     offers no evidence, however, that prices have risen faster) Tj T*
(     in India than in gold standard countries. With the exception) Tj T*
(     of Mexico, where currency conditions have become extremely) Tj T*
(     chaotic, the historical material here reprinted is in accord) Tj T*
(     with the recent monetary history of the countries under) Tj T*
