(Dollar_, which I hope to publish in 1915.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I shall begin with a skeleton statement of the plan; space is lacking) Tj T*
(for more. In brief, the plan is _virtually_ to vary each month the) Tj T*
(weight of the gold dollar, or other unit, and to vary it in such a way) Tj T*
(as to enable it always to have substantially the same general purchasing) Tj T*
(power. The word "virtually" is emphasized, lest, as has frequently) Tj T*
(happened, any one should imagine that the actual gold coins were to be) Tj T*
(recoined at a new weight each month. The simplest disposition of) Tj T*
(existing gold coins would be to call them in and issue paper) Tj T*
(certificates therefor. The virtual gold dollar would then be that) Tj T*
(varying quantum of gold _bullion_ in which each dollar of these) Tj T*
(certificates could be redeemed. The situation would be only slightly) Tj T*
(different from that at present, since very little actual gold now) Tj T*
(circulates; instead, the public uses gold certificates, obtained on the) Tj T*
(deposit of gold bullion at the Treasury, and redeemable in gold bullion) Tj T*
(at the Treasury at the rate of 25.8 grains, nine-tenths fine, per) Tj T*
(dollar. The only important change which would be introduced by the plan) Tj T*
(is in the redemption bullion; we would substitute for 25.8 a new figure) Tj T*
(each month. The gold miner, or other owners of bullion, would, just as) Tj T*
(now, deposit gold at the United States Mint or Treasury and receive) Tj T*
(paper representatives, while the jeweler, exporter, and other holders of) Tj T*
(these certificates would, just as now, present them to the Treasury when) Tj T*
(gold bullion was desired.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There would also be a small fee or "brassage," of, say, 1 per cent. for) Tj T*
("coinage," _i. e._, for depositing the bullion and obtaining its paper) Tj T*
(circulating representative. In other words, the Government would buy) Tj T*
(gold bullion at 1 per cent less than it sold it. This pair of prices,) Tj T*
(for buying and selling, would be shifted in unison, both up or both) Tj T*
(down, from month to month, it being provided, however, that no single) Tj T*
(shift should exceed 1 per cent., a figure equal to the amount by which) Tj T*
(the two differ. The object of this proviso is to prevent speculation in) Tj T*
(gold.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To determine each month what the pair of prices should be, or, what is) Tj T*
(practically the same thing, to determine what amount of gold bullion) Tj T*
(should be received and paid out in exchange for paper, recourse would be) Tj T*
(had to an official index number of prices. If, in any month, the index) Tj T*
(number is found to deviate from the initial par, the weight of bullion) Tj T*
(in which it shall be redeemable the next month is to be corrected in) Tj T*
(proportion to this deviation. Thus, the depreciation of gold would lead) Tj T*
(to a heavier virtual dollar; and an appreciation, to a lighter virtual) Tj T*
(dollar.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There are, of course, other details and possible variants of the plan,) Tj T*
