(THE NATURE AND FUNCTIONS OF TRUST COMPANIES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([91]The trust company supplements the bank. Through a long process of) Tj T*
(evolution the bank has developed as a means of facilitating the exchange) Tj T*
(of commodities. The trust company is a still further step in the same) Tj T*
(process, and, in a highly organized society, it meets needs which the) Tj T*
(bank is not able to supply.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In a new community the general store forms the centre of the business) Tj T*
(life of the place. With growth and increasing trade, the private banker) Tj T*
(sees room for the profitable employment of his funds. The state or) Tj T*
(national bank meets the needs of further growth. Success and the) Tj T*
