(It is customary for the courts to designate or approve certain trust) Tj T*
(companies as depositories for funds paid into court, and the effect of) Tj T*
(such designation or approval would be to relieve executors, trustees, or) Tj T*
(others acting in a fiduciary capacity and depositing with these) Tj T*
(companies from liability for loss through their failure. A person) Tj T*
(charged with due care in the selection of a depository could not be held) Tj T*
(to have been wanting in such care in choosing as a depository a trust) Tj T*
(company which the court has itself approved.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The powers of trust companies vary in different states, and when they) Tj T*
(are created by special legislation, local companies are found with) Tj T*
(different charter privileges. The capital and surplus of these) Tj T*
(institutions are liable for their acts in fiduciary capacities, and in) Tj T*
(some states they are required to deposit with one of the state) Tj T*
(departments a fund as a special guarantee. The liability assumed is) Tj T*
(generally accepted by the courts in lieu of the bonds which individuals) Tj T*
(acting in similar capacities are required to give.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
