(     \(13\) It does not resign.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     \(14\) All new investments of value suitable for trust estates) Tj T*
(     are offered in the first instance to trust companies, and in) Tj T*
(     that way it has a choice of valuable security; and as its) Tj T*
(     purchases are on a scale of magnitude, it can usually buy at) Tj T*
(     a rate which is lower than that at which the individual) Tj T*
(     trustee can purchase.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The most common objection to the appointment of corporate trustees is) Tj T*
(thus stated by Augustus Peabody Loring, Esq.:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     The trust companies, which have of late years become so) Tj T*
(     numerous, to a considerable extent do away with the element) Tj T*
(     of personal risk attaching to an individual trustee; but) Tj T*
(     they lack the advantages of personal management. These) Tj T*
(     companies sometimes fail from improper management as utterly) Tj T*
(     as individuals do, and as a rule the lack of personal) Tj T*
(     management results in securing the minimum return only on) Tj T*
