(POSTAL SAVINGS BANKS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The postal savings bank is not a bank, or a banking system, so much as) Tj T*
(it is an adjunct of the Government; for the fundamental idea is that) Tj T*
(through the post office the Government holds itself out as willing to) Tj T*
(accept the savings deposits of the people, invest them in its own) Tj T*
(securities and become absolutely responsible for the safe return of the) Tj T*
(funds when called for, with a nominal rate of interest. All the leading) Tj T*
(countries of the world except Germany and Switzerland now operate the) Tj T*
(postal savings banks. While the rules may differ in the details, the) Tj T*
(general scheme is the same, and a review in brief of the system of Great) Tj T*
(Britain will serve to illustrate the methods of operation of such an) Tj T*
(institution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The present system was established in England in 1861. The deposits, at) Tj T*
(whatever office they may be made, can be withdrawn from any other office) Tj T*
(which transacts a savings bank business. The accounts are kept in London) Tj T*
(and all moneys are remitted to the headquarters, where it is handed over) Tj T*
(to the Commissioners for the Reduction of the National Debt, who invest) Tj T*
(the funds in public securities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Deposits may be made as low as one shilling or multiples thereof, and) Tj T*
(the limit of deposits for an individual is $150 during one year or $650) Tj T*
(in all. Charitable societies may deposit without limit. For the benefit) Tj T*
(of youthful depositors, who have not a shilling to deposit, cards are) Tj T*
(issued upon which stamps are placed as purchased, and when filled) Tj T*
(represent one shilling, and may be turned in as cash. School managers) Tj T*
(are urged to bring this plan to the attention of the pupils, and it has) Tj T*
(been productive of good results, over 5,000 schools having adopted this) Tj T*
(system. The interest rate is fixed at 2-1/2 per cent. and never varies.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(AMERICAN POSTAL SAVINGS BANKS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARGUMENTS FOR AND AGAINST THE ESTABLISHMENT OF POSTAL SAVINGS BANKS IN) Tj T*
(THE UNITED STATES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([94]In spite of the numerous differences in the postal savings bank) Tj T*
(system of the forty-odd countries possessing them, there are certain) Tj T*
(fundamental features common to all. Whatever else a postal savings bank) Tj T*
(may be, it is without exception an institution working principally) Tj T*
(through the post offices, and its primary object is the encouragement of) Tj T*
(thrift among the poorer classes by providing safe and convenient places) Tj T*
(for the deposit of savings at a comparatively low rate of interest. In) Tj T*
(the discussion of the postal savings bank proposition in this country,) Tj T*
(no one questioned the desirability of encouraging habits of economy and) Tj T*
(thrift on the part of the public, nor was there any question that) Tj T*
(adequate savings bank facilities should be provided for this purpose;) Tj T*
(the debate hinged very largely upon the question whether adequate) Tj T*
(facilities of this character were not already provided by private) Tj T*
