(withdrawn and kept in the Treasury of the United States as reserve.) Tj T*
(Before becoming a depository, the bank must furnish as security) Tj T*
(government, state, or municipal bonds, the limit of deposits being an) Tj T*
(amount equal to the paid-up capital and one-half the surplus.... Not) Tj T*
(over 30 per cent. of the amount of such funds may be withdrawn by the) Tj T*
(trustees for investment in United States bonds, and it is the intent of) Tj T*
(the act that the residue of such funds amounting to 65 per cent., shall) Tj T*
(remain on deposit in the banks in each state and territory willing to) Tj T*
(receive the same under the terms of the act, but may be withdrawn for) Tj T*
(investment in bonds under the direction of the President, "when in his) Tj T*
(judgment, the general welfare and interests of the United States so) Tj T*
(require." Provision is also made for the conversion of savings bank) Tj T*
(deposits into United States bonds, at the request of depositors.) Tj T*
