(CHAPTER XVII) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(DOMESTIC EXCHANGE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([96]The banker has become the bookkeeper and settling agent of the) Tj T*
(business world. The products of a locality, let us say the State of) Tj T*
(Georgia, move out to the markets of the world and create credits in) Tj T*
(favor of that locality on the books of banking institutions in the) Tj T*
(commercial centers, while at the same time a counter movement of) Tj T*
(commodities is under way from other localities into Georgia, in like) Tj T*
(manner creating credits for those localities which are debits against) Tj T*
(Georgia. The practical effect is that the commodities moving between) Tj T*
(these communities are exchanged and pay for themselves, the running) Tj T*
(accounts being kept and settlements effected in the banks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To illustrate the details: A dealer in cotton in Atlanta makes a sale to) Tj T*
(a mill in Fall River and receives in payment a check or draft drawn on a) Tj T*
(New York bank, which he deposits for the credit of his account in an) Tj T*
(Atlanta bank, and which the latter forwards for the credit of its bank) Tj T*
(account in New York. Meanwhile an Atlanta merchant has bought goods in) Tj T*
(New York and in order to pay for them buys from the Atlanta bank an) Tj T*
(order for the New York credit, and this when forwarded completes the) Tj T*
(circle of payments for cotton and goods.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If we would extend the investigation to include the bank accounts of the) Tj T*
(Fall River mill and the Atlanta dealer we would find, first, that the) Tj T*
(mill account was built up constantly by deposits of checks and drafts) Tj T*
(received in payment for goods sold in all parts of the country and) Tj T*
(perhaps all over the world, with almost no deposits of cash, and that it) Tj T*
(was drawn down by checks for raw cotton, and supplies and large amounts) Tj T*
(of cash for the pay-rolls; second, that the cotton dealer's account was) Tj T*
(built up entirely by deposits of checks or drafts received for cotton) Tj T*
(shipments and drawn down by checks and cash payments to farmers for) Tj T*
(cotton.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For payments at a distance bank credit in the form of a check or draft) Tj T*
(is [commonly] used....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The foregoing illustrates the movement of the exchanges constantly) Tj T*
