(proceeding ... between ... different communities.... There is a network) Tj T*
(of relationship between banks through which each local community and) Tj T*
(market is connected with all other communities and markets.... No) Tj T*
(locality is so remote as to be outside of the circle and no community's) Tj T*
(sales and purchases are so scattered but that they can be brought) Tj T*
(together in the settlements. Each bank is the center of a circle of) Tj T*
(which it is the clearing agent; all payments between its own customers) Tj T*
(may be made by a transfer of credit upon its books. If there are two) Tj T*
(banks or more banks in a town, all payments between their customers are) Tj T*
(resolved into offsets between these banks, and in like manner all) Tj T*
(payments between localities are resolved into offsets between banks, and) Tj T*
(if not settled in local centers are passed up to larger and larger) Tj T*
(clearing centers....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But while the cross-payments of trade may be depended upon in the long) Tj T*
(run to balance and settle themselves, it does not follow that they will) Tj T*
(do so from day to day, or that they coincide so closely that payments in) Tj T*
(money are never required. An individual's sales and purchases are seldom) Tj T*
(made at the same time, and the sales and purchases of communities are) Tj T*
(not constantly balanced. The trade of a one-crop farming district will) Tj T*
(not be so evenly balanced as one of a district in which mixed farming) Tj T*
(prevails, and in every industry there are periods, usually recurring) Tj T*
(every year, when the payments exceed the current income, and) Tj T*
(corresponding periods when income exceeds outgo....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A region like the cotton states, whose products move quickly to market,) Tj T*
(may have large credit balances at one season and at another be wanting) Tj T*
(to borrow....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The banker is an equalizing agency in the situation. He stands in the) Tj T*
(breach: he must either supply the missing offsets of credit, or, as a) Tj T*
(last resort, make the payments in money....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The entire system of settlements, with transfers and offsets and) Tj T*
(advances and interchange of capital and credit, is exceedingly) Tj T*
(interesting and wonderfully simple and effective, but depends for its) Tj T*
(effectiveness upon a scrupulous observance of the principle upon which) Tj T*
(it is based. That principle is the natural reciprocity of trade....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(While there are balances from time to time in the exchanges ... between) Tj T*
(different localities ... which cannot be settled without shipments of) Tj T*
(money, they are usually met without inconvenience unless there is a) Tj T*
(disturbance of credit.) Tj T*
