(of realizing a fair price. As the sale of a bill, moreover, carries the) Tj T*
(valuable advantage of ready money and a speedy turnover of capital, it) Tj T*
(is invariably preferred by the foreign exporter, who has consigned or) Tj T*
(sold produce to us, to the alternative plan of awaiting remittances from) Tj T*
(this side. The foreign importer, too, who has to pay for the goods he) Tj T*
(has bought, would rather do so by remitting to London than by allowing) Tj T*
(us to draw upon him. In the former case, the rate he has to pay depends) Tj T*
(upon his own success in higgling; in the latter, it is fixed by a London) Tj T*
(bill-broker, who has not the same interest in the matter.) Tj T*
