(merchant to the extent of relieving him of the tribute formerly paid to) Tj T*
(the indirect channels of liquidation, or, in other words, to the foreign) Tj T*
(banker.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Dollar Credit is of capital importance to every American merchant) Tj T*
(who is interested either directly or indirectly in the importation of) Tj T*
(commodities of any character. A study of the advantages accruing from) Tj T*
(this form of credit will demonstrate the desirability of its general) Tj T*
(employment as the vehicle for financing not only our own imports but) Tj T*
(also those of other countries. Primarily, it is more economical than the) Tj T*
(Sterling or Continental Credit, for the initial commission cost of) Tj T*
(issuance is lower. Secondly, it is based on a known quantity, the) Tj T*
(dollar, a factor of supreme importance in these days of extreme and) Tj T*
(violent fluctuations in the exchange rates, and therefore all exchange) Tj T*
(risk is eliminated from the operation as far as the importer is) Tj T*
