(THE NEW YORK FOREIGN EXCHANGE MARKET[114]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A market may be defined as the coming together of buyers and sellers. It) Tj T*
(therefore involves all the mechanism necessary to facilitate their) Tj T*
(intercourse. One may speak of a general market or of a local market, of) Tj T*
(a market in one or in another place. Thus, there is the New York market) Tj T*
(for the buying and selling of exchange on London. A bank in New Haven,) Tj T*
(Connecticut, may be a part of that market if it buys from and sells to) Tj T*
(it. That market includes, besides the commercial and industrial) Tj T*
(organizations which buy or sell drafts, all middlemen of whatever class) Tj T*
(who engage in the trade.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The middlemen may be divided roughly into three classes. First may be) Tj T*
(mentioned banks which do a regular foreign exchange business, buying) Tj T*
(bills from those who have them to sell and selling their own drafts on) Tj T*
