() Tj T*
(The ratio of balances to clearings depends partly upon the number of) Tj T*
(banks, but much more upon the amount and character of their business and) Tj T*
(upon their relations one to another. This is illustrated by figures) Tj T*
(which have just been collected, covering the transactions for the year) Tj T*
(1908. At Pittsburg, with 20 members and 128 non-members clearing through) Tj T*
(members, the balances were 16.5 per cent. of the clearings; at Buffalo,) Tj T*
(with 11 members and 7 non-members, 12 per cent.; at Chicago, with 20) Tj T*
(members and 40 non-members clearing through members, 7.5 per cent.; at) Tj T*
(Philadelphia, with 31 members and 1 non-member, 11.5 per cent.; at St.) Tj T*
(Louis, with 17 members and 35 non-members, 9.3 per cent.; while in New) Tj T*
(York, during the fifty-four years of its existence, the percentage of) Tj T*
(balances to clearings has been only 4.64 per cent., notwithstanding the) Tj T*
(operation of the United States assistant treasurer, who almost always) Tj T*
(has a heavy debit balance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
