(The loan certificates are taken out by the clearing-house members) Tj T*
(through loan committees, specially appointed, and are used, as a rule,) Tj T*
(only in the payment of balances among the associated banks. Thus, when) Tj T*
(the stringency in the money market seems sufficient to demand it, the) Tj T*
(clearing-house association meets and appoints a committee called the) Tj T*
("loan committee," consisting usually of five bank officers, to act in) Tj T*
(concurrence with the president of the clearing-house association, who) Tj T*
(serves ex officio as a member. It is the duty of such committee to meet) Tj T*
(each morning at the clearing house and examine the collateral offered as) Tj T*
(security by the banks and issue loan certificates thereon, in such) Tj T*
(denominations and proportions to collaterals deposited as may be agreed) Tj T*
(upon. In the past the denominations have varied from 25 cents to) Tj T*
($100,000 in the different associations and in proportions varying from) Tj T*
($50 to $100 of certificates to $100 of collateral deposited.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These loan certificates bear interest at rates varying from 5 to 10 per) Tj T*
(cent. per annum, payable by the banks to which they are issued to the) Tj T*
(banks receiving such certificates in settlement of daily balances. Hence) Tj T*
(the interest charged against certain banks must exactly equal and offset) Tj T*
(that credited to certain other banks. The aim is to fix the rates) Tj T*
(sufficiently high to insure the retirement of the certificates as soon) Tj T*
(as the emergency which called them forth has passed by. As a rule they) Tj T*
(are retired by the banks, which take them out as soon as they have) Tj T*
(obtained sufficient cash to meet their daily obligations. Notice is) Tj T*
(given by the debtor banks to the committee, calling for such) Tj T*
(certificates as they wish to retire, and the committee gives notice to) Tj T*
(the banks holding the same, stating that the interest will cease after a) Tj T*
(specified date. In due course the holders send the certificates to the) Tj T*
(clearing house for redemption. Upon the retirement of the certificates) Tj T*
(the collateral deposited as security is surrendered by the committee in) Tj T*
(the same proportion to certificates turned in as was required for) Tj T*
(deposit at the time of issue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is by no means the general practice for all the members to take out) Tj T*
(loan certificates when issues are arranged by the association. Some) Tj T*
