(In 1873 the New York banks at the outset of the crisis held an available) Tj T*
(reserve of $34,300,000. In the course of four weeks this was reduced to) Tj T*
($5,800,000, and the ratio to deposit liabilities was then less than 4.5) Tj T*
(per cent.[130] Suspension was not escaped in 1873 but it was of shorter) Tj T*
(duration than in later crises. The banks at that time were unable to) Tj T*
(increase their cash resources by any of the means which have been) Tj T*
(available in later crises. The Government had no surplus of greenbacks,) Tj T*
