(retained by the savings banks. Banknotes could not be issued because the) Tj T*
(total circulation was at that time limited by law. Finally, additional) Tj T*
(supplies of gold, secured through imports, were useless for ordinary) Tj T*
(banking purposes because the business of the country was then carried on) Tj T*
(by means of an inconvertible and depreciated paper currency.) Tj T*
(Notwithstanding all these special difficulties, the New York banks, by) Tj T*
(continuing to use their reserves freely even after payments had been) Tj T*
(restricted, were able to restore confidence in a comparatively short) Tj T*
(time, and money began to flow back to them within three weeks after the) Tj T*
(outbreak of the crisis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1893 the New York banks were in what was for them an unusually strong) Tj T*
