(cash reserve exceeding 30 per cent. of their net deposits. A succession) Tj T*
(of banking failures in the West and South led to heavy withdrawals from) Tj T*
(New York during the latter part of June and the beginning of July. Then) Tj T*
(followed a lull and money began to be returned to New York. During the) Tj T*
(third week of July banking failures were renewed in the West and South) Tj T*
(and the drain was resumed. The positively unfavorable aspects of the) Tj T*
(situation were altogether similar to those of the previous month with) Tj T*
(the one further circumstance of a reduced cash reserve in New York. On) Tj T*
(the other hand, additional means with which to meet the situation were) Tj T*
(becoming available. At the end of July gold imports in large amount had) Tj T*
(been arranged. Foreign purchases of our securities were heavy,) Tj T*
(reflecting increasing confidence in the repeal of the silver purchase) Tj T*
(law. Arrangements had also been made which would certainly lead to a) Tj T*
(considerable increase in the issues of bank-notes during August and) Tj T*
(September. Notwithstanding all these favorable circumstances the New) Tj T*
(York banks suspended, during the first week of August, when they still) Tj T*
(held a cash reserve of $79,000,000, more than 20 per cent. of their) Tj T*
(deposit liabilities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1907 the New York banks restricted payments when they still held a) Tj T*
(cash reserve of more than $220,000,000 and when the reserve ratio was) Tj T*
(also above 20 per cent. Both in 1893 and in 1907 suspension was not a) Tj T*
(measure of last resort taken after the banks had entirely exhausted) Tj T*
(their reserves and when there was no means of securing additional cash) Tj T*
(resources. Moreover, after cash payments were restricted the policy of) Tj T*
(the banks was unlike that adopted in 1873, in that the banks did not) Tj T*
(make further use of their reserves; they hoarded them and added to their) Tj T*
(amount, thus unduly prolonging the period of suspension.) Tj T*
