(In substantially his own words the Chicago examiner operates under the) Tj T*
(following conditions: The examinations extend to all the associated) Tj T*
(banks of Chicago and to all non-member institutions. The work is) Tj T*
(conducted with the aid of five regular assistants, each fitted by) Tj T*
(experience to thoroughly do that part of the work assigned to him. The) Tj T*
(examinations include, besides a verification of the assets and) Tj T*
(liabilities of each bank, so far as is possible, an investigation into) Tj T*
(the workings of every department and are made as thorough as is) Tj T*
(practicable. After each examination the examiner prepares a detailed) Tj T*
(report in duplicate, describing the bank's loans, bonds, investments,) Tj T*
(and other assets, mentioning specially all loans, either direct or) Tj T*
(indirect, to officers, directors, or employees, or to corporations in) Tj T*
(which they may be interested. The report also contains a description of) Tj T*
(conditions found in every department. One of these reports is filed in) Tj T*
(the vaults of the clearing house, in the custody of the examiner, and) Tj T*
(the other is handed to the examined bank's president for the use of its) Tj T*
(directors. The individual directors are then notified that the) Tj T*
(examination has been made and that a copy of the examiner's report has) Tj T*
(been handed to the president for their use. In this way every director) Tj T*
(is given an opportunity to see the report, and the examiner, in every) Tj T*
(instance, insists upon receiving acknowledgment of the receipt of these) Tj T*
(notices.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The detailed report retained by the examiner is not submitted to the) Tj T*
(clearing-house committee, under whose direct supervision he operates,) Tj T*
(unless the discovery of unusual conditions makes it necessary. A special) Tj T*
(report in brief form is prepared in every case and read to the) Tj T*
(clearing-house committee at meetings called for that purpose. The report) Tj T*
(is made in letter form, and describes in general terms the character of) Tj T*
(the examined bank's assets, points out all loans, direct or indirect, to) Tj T*
(officers, directors, or employees, or to corporations in which they may) Tj T*
(have an interest. It further describes all excessive and important) Tj T*
(loans, calls attention to any unwarranted conditions, gross) Tj T*
(irregularities, or dangerous tendencies, should any such exist, and) Tj T*
(expresses, in a general way, the examiner's opinion of each bank as he) Tj T*
