(use of one of three methods: \(1\) By special charter; \(2\) under the) Tj T*
("business incorporation law"; \(3\) under the general banking law. Not) Tj T*
(very many of the States have used consecutively all three methods, for) Tj T*
(the special charter and the "business incorporation law" were used) Tj T*
(contemporaneously in different sections of the country. Both have given) Tj T*
(place, in the great mass of States, to the general banking law. From) Tj T*
(1865 to 1875 probably the greater number of the banks formed were) Tj T*
(incorporated under special acts; from 1875 to 1887 incorporation under) Tj T*
(the "business incorporation law" was the prevailing method, and since) Tj T*
(then the general banking law has become the almost universal method of) Tj T*
(incorporating banks and trust companies.) Tj T*
