(out, profit can be obtained only by making loans. These when greater) Tj T*
(than the amount of the capital, as it is necessary that they should be,) Tj T*
(can be made by the loan of funds left with banks by others or by the) Tj T*
(issue of circulating notes. It is also clear that, were the) Tj T*
(possibilities of loaning beyond the amount of the capital wholly or) Tj T*
(chiefly confined to one of these forms of liability--the other being) Tj T*
(unavailable, as in the case of the state bank notes whose issue is) Tj T*
(prohibited by the 10 per cent. tax--and were this other form distasteful) Tj T*
(or impossible of introduction among the community where the branch was) Tj T*
(to be established, the motive for the creation of the branch would be) Tj T*
(absent. This motive has been wanting in many parts of the United States.) Tj T*
(By the laws of the United States, the issue of notes has been made) Tj T*
(impossible to all save national banks, and the capital of these banks) Tj T*
(has been limited to $50,000 as a minimum. Banks other than national) Tj T*
(must, therefore, be established under state laws, some of which have) Tj T*
(permitted the organization of such institutions with capitals as low as) Tj T*
($5,000 or $10,000. They can, however, make use only of deposits as a) Tj T*
