(The reserve requirements are made still more definite by the fact that) Tj T*
(the law compels the banks to keep one-half at least of the reserve on) Tj T*
(hand in "gold, gold bullion, gold coin, United States gold certificates,) Tj T*
(or United States notes: and the remainder in any form of currency) Tj T*
(authorized by the law of the United States other than federal reserve) Tj T*
(notes.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Among the powers granted to these banks is the power "to accept for) Tj T*
(payment at a future date, drafts drawn upon its customers and to issue) Tj T*
(letters of credit authorizing the holders thereof to draw drafts upon it) Tj T*
(or its correspondents at sight or on time not exceeding one year." This) Tj T*
(clause gives a much wider power to the state banks in the important) Tj T*
(matter of acceptances than its counterpart in the Federal Reserve Act.) Tj T*
(In the one case both domestic and foreign acceptances may be made and) Tj T*
(handled without stipulation as to aggregate amount and bearing) Tj T*
(maturities of one year or less, while in the other case the acceptances) Tj T*
(are limited to those arising out of the importation or exportation of) Tj T*
(goods with maturities not exceeding six months. Seemingly, the state) Tj T*
(banks have the advantage, and to this extent the state law is superior) Tj T*
(to the federal act.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One other important forward step was taken in relation to this group of) Tj T*
(banks. They are given the privilege of establishing branches outside) Tj T*
(the State of New York, either in the United States or in foreign) Tj T*
(countries. This privilege is qualified, however, by the provision that) Tj T*
(no bank can establish such branches unless it has a combined capital and) Tj T*
(surplus of $1,000,000 or over and the written approval of the) Tj T*
(superintendent of banks. Although the old law permitted trust companies) Tj T*
(to establish branches in the place where they were incorporated, the) Tj T*
(practical effect was to limit branch banking to the city of New York. In) Tj T*
(this particular also the state banks have the advantage over the banks) Tj T*
(in the federal reserve system which are allowed to establish branches) Tj T*
(only in foreign countries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _Features relating to private banks and bankers._ The regulation of) Tj T*
(private banks and bankers is an entirely new departure in the law of) Tj T*
(this State. In the past the banking department had no authority to) Tj T*
(supervise that relatively large number of private bankers who receive) Tj T*
(deposits in small amounts from the wage-earning classes while conducting) Tj T*
(in connection therewith a mercantile or some other kind of business.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Mercantile firms like the Siegel Company, by paying a higher rate of) Tj T*
(interest upon deposits than savings banks, were able to obtain the) Tj T*
(savings of many small depositors. This money was invested in the) Tj T*
(business and secured only by the capital stock of the mercantile) Tj T*
(establishments. In case the firm failed there was no security back of) Tj T*
(these deposits but these same shares of stock, and so depositors were) Tj T*
(fortunate if they received in settlement even 40 per cent. of their) Tj T*
(claims. Such firms were not doing a legitimate banking business inasmuch) Tj T*
(as they did not keep their assets in liquid form and carried no reserve) Tj T*
