(against deposits.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The new act corrects this situation by giving the banking department) Tj T*
(authority to conduct independent investigations into any violation of) Tj T*
(the banking law by a corporation or individual. In the future a) Tj T*
(corporation which is in any way engaged in the business of banking) Tj T*
(cannot hide under the wing of the general corporation law when the) Tj T*
(banking department sees fit to make an investigation of its affairs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Some of the specifications of this part of the law are all securities,) Tj T*
(property, and the evidences of title thereto in which the permanent) Tj T*
(capital and the deposits are invested are to be segregated and kept) Tj T*
(separate from all other property and assets of the private banker;) Tj T*
(depositors have a prior lien on the assets of the private banker, in) Tj T*
(case of insolvency or suspension of business; and, in addition, every) Tj T*
(private banker must maintain a reserve of 15 per cent. against deposits) Tj T*
(in cities of the first class and a reserve of 10 per cent. in any other) Tj T*
(city, one-tenth of which shall consist of reserve on hand and the) Tj T*
(remainder may be kept on deposit subject to call with banks approved by) Tj T*
(the superintendent of banks. These requirements will go far toward) Tj T*
(preventing the recurrence of such disasters as the Siegel failure.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. _Features relating to co-operative credit._ Within the last thirty) Tj T*
(years the agricultural methods of the State, in harmony with the) Tj T*
(agricultural methods throughout the United States, have undergone great) Tj T*
(changes. Scientific farming, improved machinery, and changed market) Tj T*
(conditions have brought new problems in the field of agricultural) Tj T*
(credit. To-day agriculture has come to be in a real sense capitalistic) Tj T*
(and has in consequence laid new requirements on the credit structure of) Tj T*
(the nation. Moreover, the period of large returns or satisfactory) Tj T*
(returns from an extensive and rather careless cultivation of the soil,) Tj T*
(which made possible an ignoring of unit cost, or, at least, brought the) Tj T*
(farmer to minimize the importance of such cost, has given way, so far as) Tj T*
(the successful farmer is concerned, to the careful estimates of cost and) Tj T*
(close calculations of profits on a narrow margin between unit cost and) Tj T*
(unit selling price.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the field of cost, the rate at which capital or money may be borrowed) Tj T*
(is no small factor; and with the high rates prevailing in the United) Tj T*
(States in comparison with those current in Europe, the borrower in this) Tj T*
(country who pledges his land or agricultural products as security for a) Tj T*
(loan finds himself at a disadvantage. To meet this condition cheaper) Tj T*
(agricultural credit has been strongly urged. Europe furnishes the) Tj T*
(example in her well-organized land banks and co-operative credit unions.) Tj T*
(Already Massachusetts has a law authorizing co-operative organizations) Tj T*
(for furnishing cheaper credit facilities to the agriculturalist, and in) Tj T*
(Illinois there is a "credit foncier" which has been in successful) Tj T*
(operation a number of years. New York State has put itself in line with) Tj T*
(this growing movement to furnish ample and cheaper credit to the farmer) Tj T*
(and the purchasers of real estate by putting into the new law provisions) Tj T*
(for the establishment of a land bank and co-operative credit unions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
