(Sections 421-438 authorize ten or more savings and loan associations,) Tj T*
(the aggregate resources of which shall not be less than $5,000,000, to) Tj T*
(form a Land Bank of the State of New York. This bank can "issue, sell) Tj T*
(and redeem debenture bonds secured by bonds and first mortgages made to) Tj T*
(or held by member associations" and "invest its capital and other funds) Tj T*
(in bonds secured by first mortgages on real estate situated within the) Tj T*
(territory in which its members are authorized to make loans." The bank) Tj T*
(is not permitted to do a general deposit business or incur any) Tj T*
(indebtedness upon notes and bonds in excess of twenty times the amount) Tj T*
(of its capital. The debenture bonds authorized by the act are to be) Tj T*
(issued in series of not less than $50,000, and may be called on any) Tj T*
(interest day at 102-1/2 provided a sixty-day notice is given.) Tj T*
(Amortization payments upon mortgages which are given as collateral) Tj T*
(security for the debentures of the land bank shall be sufficient to) Tj T*
(liquidate the debt in a period not exceeding forty years.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In Article XI the law provides for the establishment of credit unions. A) Tj T*
(credit union may be organized by any seven or more persons with a share) Tj T*
(capital the par value of which shall not exceed $25. The objects of the) Tj T*
(credit union are: \(1\) to loan money in small amounts on personal) Tj T*
(security or in larger amounts on endorsed notes at rates not exceeding 1) Tj T*
(per cent. per month, inclusive of all charges incident to the making of) Tj T*
(such loans; \(2\) to receive the savings of its members in payment of) Tj T*
(shares on deposit; \(3\) to borrow money to an amount not to exceed 40 per) Tj T*
(cent. of its capital; \(4\) to pay dividends on its share capital. As to) Tj T*
(the method of making loans, the law prescribes that a credit committee) Tj T*
(shall pass upon all applications for loans which must be made in writing) Tj T*
(and must state the purpose for which the loan is desired and the) Tj T*
(security offered. No loan will be made unless it receives the unanimous) Tj T*
(approval of the members of the committee present at the meeting,) Tj T*
(provided always a majority of the committee is present.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(With the land bank acting as a central clearing agency for the local) Tj T*
(savings and loan associations and the organization of many rural credit) Tj T*
(unions the problem of agricultural credit will be largely solved for New) Tj T*
(York State. This, however, all hinges on the proper functioning of the) Tj T*
(land bank and the co-operation of the farmers in the establishment of) Tj T*
(local credit unions. Agriculturists as a class are slow to adopt new) Tj T*
(methods and it may be only after prolonged education that all the) Tj T*
(possibilities of this new legislation will be realized.) Tj T*
