stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(is little that is radically new in the Canadian system. He finds in it) Tj T*
(many of the practices and expedients that were found excellent in the) Tj T*
(United States in the first half of the nineteenth century, and is almost) Tj T*
(persuaded that but for the Civil War what is now known as the Canadian) Tj T*
(banking system would everywhere be called the American system.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fiscal exigencies of war, which have caused changes in the banking) Tj T*
(systems of most countries, have had no influence upon the development of) Tj T*
(banking in Canada. During the first half of the nineteenth century the) Tj T*
(commercial and financial interests of Canada and the United States were) Tj T*
(comparatively intimate and the financial institutions of both countries) Tj T*
(developed on similar lines. The safety-fund system, first introduced in) Tj T*
(the State of New York in 1829, found favor also in Canada and is still) Tj T*
(an integral part of the Canadian banking system. Branch banking, which) Tj T*
(was most successfully illustrated in this country by the State Bank of) Tj T*
(Indiana, and which now exists in some form or other in almost all) Tj T*
(countries except the United States, has always prevailed in Canada. The) Tj T*
(importance of a prompt redemption of bank notes as exemplified in the) Tj T*
(old Suffolk banking system in New England before the war, was fully) Tj T*
(realized in Canada and is probably better illustrated in the present) Tj T*
(Canadian system than in any other country. There bank notes and bank) Tj T*
(checks are treated as identical in nature, both being cleared with the) Tj T*
(same regularity and promptness. The so-called free banking system, which) Tj T*
(was first adopted in the State of New York in 1839 and thereafter) Tj T*
(adopted by eighteen other States of the Union, was tried in Canada in) Tj T*
(the fifties, but not on a large scale. This system, requiring that) Tj T*
(issues of bank notes should be secured by a segregated deposit of) Tj T*
(certain classes of stocks and bonds, has never met with approval among) Tj T*
(the leading bankers of Canada.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Canadian system is a product of evolution. It has taken its present) Tj T*
(form because of the commercial and financial needs of the Canadian) Tj T*
(people. It was not created by lawyers or statesmen to meet a fiscal need) Tj T*
(of the Government, but has grown up gradually under the fostering care) Tj T*
(of experienced bankers, no changes having been made until experience) Tj T*
(proved them necessary or advisable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The chartered banks transact the business which in the United States is) Tj T*
(divided among national banks, trust companies, private banks, and) Tj T*
(savings banks. They buy and sell commercial paper, discount the notes of) Tj T*
(their customers, lend money on stocks and bonds, make advances to) Tj T*
(farmers, and sometimes aid in the financing of railroads and industrial) Tj T*
(enterprises. To a Canadian the word "bank" means one of the twenty-odd) Tj T*
("chartered banks," for the law prohibits the use of the word "bank" by) Tj T*
(any other institution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(OTHER FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The only other financial institutions in Canada which possess much) Tj T*
(importance are the mortgage and loan companies. These usually operate) Tj T*
(under charters granted by the provincial legislatures and do a business) Tj T*
