stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(similar to that of the farm and mortgage companies which once flourished) Tj T*
(in the United States, making loans to farmers for a term of years and) Tj T*
(taking farm mortgage for security. They also make loans upon urban and) Tj T*
(suburban real estate and thus aid in the upbuilding of the cities and) Tj T*
(their suburbs. The business of these institutions is made possible by) Tj T*
(the fact that the bank act does not permit the chartered banks to accept) Tj T*
(loans secured by real estate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Dominion Government maintains a double system of savings banks. One) Tj T*
(set is managed by the post-office department, every post-office) Tj T*
(receiving deposits. The other set is managed by the finance department.) Tj T*
(The post-office department also sells annuities and old-age pensions.) Tj T*
(The money received through the savings banks is regarded as a loan from) Tj T*
(the people and is used, like money obtained by taxation, in the payment) Tj T*
(of the Government's general expenses. The Government is required to) Tj T*
(carry a gold reserve of 10 per cent. against the savings deposits, but) Tj T*
(no assets are set aside for their security. The chartered banks pay the) Tj T*
(same rate of interest and get most of the business, for they offer) Tj T*
(facilities with which the Government does not attempt to compete. Most) Tj T*
(of the Government's deposits come from the poorest and most ignorant) Tj T*
(classes, people who in all countries are suspicious of banks. Some of) Tj T*
(the Canadian cities maintain municipal savings banks, but they are of) Tj T*
(relatively small importance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Trust companies in Canada are not financial institutions. They are) Tj T*
(trust companies in fact as well as in name, their business being to act) Tj T*
(as trustee and administrator. A few of them accept deposits, although it) Tj T*
(is not certain that they have a right to do so. The bulk of the money) Tj T*
(they handle comes to them through the administration of estates and) Tj T*
(trust funds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Private banking firms are almost unknown in Canada, there being only two) Tj T*
(or three in the entire Dominion, and these do a mortgage and loan) Tj T*
(business rather than a strictly commercial banking business.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Hence, if any one seeks to understand the financial or banking situation) Tj T*
(in Canada, he must devote his attention in the main to the chartered) Tj T*
(banks. These through their branches furnish the loanable capital) Tj T*
(necessary for the support of the Dominion's trade and industry and for) Tj T*
(much of its agricultural enterprise. To them the Government turns when) Tj T*
(funds are needed for internal improvements or when the exchequer faces a) Tj T*
(deficit. The promoters of street railways, steam railways, steam) Tj T*
(railroads, and other permanent improvements take counsel with the) Tj T*
(managers of these chartered banks before they issue their securities.) Tj T*
(The banks as a rule do not invest their funds in the stocks or bonds of) Tj T*
(new enterprises, yet their managers are the men most familiar with the) Tj T*
(world's money markets and their approval, therefore, of any financial) Tj T*
(undertaking is highly esteemed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE ESSENTIALS OF THE SYSTEM) Tj T*
() Tj T*
