(A chartered bank in Canada is a bank of branches, not a bank with) Tj T*
(branches. The parent bank, technically known as the "head office,") Tj T*
(neither takes deposits nor lends money. All the banking business is done) Tj T*
(by the branches, each enjoying considerable independence, but all) Tj T*
(subject to the supervision and control of the head office. The law) Tj T*
(places no restrictions upon the number or location of branches. Canadian) Tj T*
(banks, therefore, have branches in foreign countries as well as in) Tj T*
(Canada.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PROCESS OF INCORPORATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The provisions of the bank act with respect to the organization of new) Tj T*
(banks are intended to guard against the entry of unfit or inexperienced) Tj T*
(persons into the banking business. The minimum required capital of a) Tj T*
(bank is $500,000, of which all must be subscribed and one-half paid in) Tj T*
(before a new bank can open. At least five men of integrity and good) Tj T*
(financial standing must agree to act as provisional directors and secure) Tj T*
(a favorable report on their project from the parliamentary committee on) Tj T*
(banking and commerce. These men must agree to subscribe for fairly large) Tj T*
(blocks of stock, otherwise the committee will be inclined to reject) Tj T*
(their application. They must convince the committee that their project) Tj T*
(is a well considered one, that there is need for the new bank. If they) Tj T*
(satisfy the parliamentary committee it will be granted. The bank,) Tj T*
(however, cannot yet begin business. Provisional directors now have) Tj T*
(merely the right to advertise and cause stock books to be opened. If) Tj T*
(inside of one year capital stock to the amount of $500,000 has been) Tj T*
(subscribed and $250,000 thereof paid in, the provisional directors may) Tj T*
(call a meeting of the shareholders, at which a board of regular) Tj T*
(directors shall be chosen. Before this meeting is held at least $250,000) Tj T*
(in cash must be paid over to the Minister of Finance. The regular) Tj T*
(directors must then apply to a body known as the treasury board for a) Tj T*
(certificate permitting the bank to issue notes and begin business and) Tj T*
(the treasury board may refuse this certificate unless it is entirely) Tj T*
(satisfied that all the requirements of the law have been met. Delay on) Tj T*
(the part of the treasury board might prove fatal to the new enterprise,) Tj T*
(for if a new bank does not obtain a certificate within one year from the) Tj T*
(date of its incorporation, all the rights, powers, and privileges) Tj T*
(conferred by the act of incorporation cease. These requirements make it) Tj T*
(impossible to organize a new bank in Canada with any degree of secrecy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(NOTE ISSUES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Having obtained its charter, a new bank must open its head office in the) Tj T*
(place designated, and may then proceed to establish branches or) Tj T*
(agencies, upon the number and location of which the law places no) Tj T*
(restriction. Under its charter it has authority to issue circulating) Tj T*
(notes up to the amount of its unimpaired paid-up capital in) Tj T*
(denominations of $5 and multiples thereof. An amendment of the bank act) Tj T*
(passed July 20, 1908, gives the bank the right to issue what may be) Tj T*
(called an emergency circulation during the crop-moving season \(October 1) Tj T*
ET
