(THE REVISION OF THE BANK ACT, 1913[148]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Canadian Bank Act, as is well known, is subject to decennial) Tj T*
(revision. The last revision was due to take place in 1910; but owing to) Tj T*
(circumstances which it is not necessary here to describe, it was not) Tj T*
(until the present year that the work was finally undertaken. The leading) Tj T*
(features of the Canadian banking system are so well known that they may) Tj T*
(be passed over, and the nature and causes of the recent changes in the) Tj T*
(act alone described. There were many minor modifications, but the) Tj T*
(essential changes effected were: \(1\) provision for a shareholders') Tj T*
(audit, \(2\) the creation of central gold reserves, and \(3\) the providing) Tj T*
(of additional facilities for making loans to farmers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the recent revision of the act the public was most deeply concerned) Tj T*
(with the problem of securing an adequate system of bank inspection. The) Tj T*
