BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(immediate reason for this was the disastrous failure of the Farmers') Tj T*
(Bank. This institution had gambled away its resources on the Keeley) Tj T*
(mine; and had, in its failure, brought many farmers as well as others to) Tj T*
(the verge of ruin. For several years previous, however, there had been) Tj T*
(an insistent demand for some sort of external bank inspection....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The banks as a whole have been opposed to any change in the method of) Tj T*
(inspection. The reason they advance is that the keynote of the) Tj T*
(organization of Canadian banks has always been the centralization of) Tj T*
(responsibility; and they do not think it wise to divide that) Tj T*
(responsibility with any outside authority....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As far as the public is concerned it has no means of judging of the) Tj T*
(soundness of a bank except by examining the monthly returns which are) Tj T*
(required by law from each bank. These returns are fairly comprehensive,) Tj T*
(and have been made more so by the revision of the act this year. The) Tj T*
(Minister of Finance may call for supplementary information from any) Tj T*
(bank, whenever, in his judgment, such data are required to afford a) Tj T*
(fuller knowledge of a bank's affairs. Of course, these returns can be) Tj T*
(taken only for what they are worth. In the case of several failed banks) Tj T*
(the returns were made with every degree of falsification, because no) Tj T*
(independent checking of the figures was possible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Nevertheless, in obedience to the strong demand for some sort of) Tj T*
(independent bank examination, provision was made in the recent revision) Tj T*
(of the act for a shareholders' audit of each bank's affairs. The) Tj T*
(auditors are to be chosen by the shareholders from a list of forty names) Tj T*
(selected by the whole body of the general managers of the banks. The) Tj T*
(list must be submitted to the Minister of Finance for his approval. If) Tj T*
(one-third of the shareholders of a bank are dissatisfied with the) Tj T*
(auditor appointed by the majority, they may appeal to the Minister for) Tj T*
(the appointment of another auditor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The auditors must submit a statement of their findings to the) Tj T*
(shareholders at the annual meeting, or on any other occasion the) Tj T*
(necessity may require. In addition the Minister of Finance may require a) Tj T*
(special return to be made to him, the cost of the service rendered being) Tj T*
(paid for by the Government.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Canadians would be wise not to expect too much from this system of) Tj T*
(external examination. After all, it can do no more than verify a bank's) Tj T*
(statements and books.... In every large undertaking, the soundness of) Tj T*
(the transaction must depend, as before, upon the judgment of the general) Tj T*
(manager and the board of directors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The establishment of central gold reserves is the most important feature) Tj T*
(added to Canada's banking system by the legislation of 1913.... Under) Tj T*
(the new act each bank may issue any amount of notes that it may desire,) Tj T*
(provided that it deposits with a board of trustees, at Montreal, gold or) Tj T*
(Dominion notes to the full amount of the notes issued. These notes are) Tj T*
(to be identical in form with the ordinary notes of the bank. The gold or) Tj T*
(Dominion notes deposited with the trustees shall be returned to the bank) Tj T*
