(     Be it therefore declared and enacted, that any body politic) Tj T*
(     or corporate, or society, or company, or partnership,) Tj T*
(     although consisting of more than six persons, may carry on) Tj T*
(     the trade or business of banking in London, or within) Tj T*
(     sixty-five miles thereof, provided that such body politic or) Tj T*
(     corporate, or society, or company, or partnership, do not) Tj T*
(     borrow, owe or take up in England, any sum or sums of money) Tj T*
(     on their bills or notes payable on demand, or at any less) Tj T*
(     time than six months from the borrowing thereof, during the) Tj T*
(     continuance of the privileges granted by this Act to the) Tj T*
(     said Governor and Company of the Bank of England.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It may be noted that this act of 1833 constituted Bank of England notes) Tj T*
(a legal tender, except by the bank itself or its branches....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PEEL'S ACT OR THE BANK CHARTER ACT OF 1844, AND ITS SUSPENSIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([151]After the renewal of the charter in 1833, the directors of the Bank) Tj T*
(of England laid down as a principle on which their future operations) Tj T*
(were to be guided, that one-third of their liabilities should be kept in) Tj T*
(cash and bullion, and the remaining two-thirds in securities. If this) Tj T*
(principle had been acted on, the bank would have been saved from many of) Tj T*
(the troubles which shortly assailed it; but though the intentions of the) Tj T*
(directors were good, circumstances were too strong for them, and the) Tj T*
(actual proportions of cash and securities to liabilities, respectively,) Tj T*
(often differed materially from the standard laid down. This was notably) Tj T*
(the case during the periods of financial pressure which were experienced) Tj T*
(in the years 1836 and 1837.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the year 1839 matters assumed a very serious aspect. In the early) Tj T*
(part of this year the amount of cash held by the bank was about) Tj T*
(one-third of the amount of securities, but during the year the amount) Tj T*
(invested in securities increased at the expense of the amount held in) Tj T*
(cash; and by September we find that securities stood at nearly) Tj T*
(L29,000,000, while the cash was reduced to a tenth of that figure, and) Tj T*
(stood at L2,936,000 only. In order to avert a calamity which appeared to) Tj T*
(be impending, the bank arranged loans in Paris and Hamburg to the extent) Tj T*
(of between three and four millions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This manifest exhibition of weakness on the part of the bank led to the) Tj T*
(appointment of a committee of the House of Commons to inquire into the) Tj T*
(matter. The committee condemned the principles on which the bank was) Tj T*
(working, but were powerless to effect any alteration, owing to the) Tj T*
(charter of the bank not expiring till 1844.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the expiry of the charter, however, Sir Robert Peel brought forward) Tj T*
(his famous act for remodelling the bank, and regulating the issues of) Tj T*
(the country banks throughout. England and Wales.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The act was passed on the 19th July, 1844, and continues without) Tj T*
(alteration to the present day. The main provisions enacted thereby,) Tj T*
ET
endstream
