stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(briefly stated, are as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I. The issue department and the ordinary banking department of the Bank) Tj T*
(of England were to be entirely separated as from the 31st August, 1844.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(II. On such separation taking place, securities to the value of) Tj T*
(L14,000,000 \(including the [book] debt due to the bank from the) Tj T*
(Government\) were to be transferred to the issue department, together) Tj T*
(with so much gold coin and bullion that the total so transferred should) Tj T*
(equal the total amount of notes then outstanding. Thereafter \(with the) Tj T*
(exception noted below\) the issue department must not issue any notes in) Tj T*
(excess of a total of L14,000,000 except in exchange for gold coin or) Tj T*
(bullion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(III. The issue department might not at any time hold more silver than) Tj T*
(one-fourth part of the gold held. As a matter of fact the issue) Tj T*
(department holds no silver.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IV. Notes might be demanded from the issue department by any person in) Tj T*
(exchange for gold at the rate of L3 17_s._ 9_d._ per standard ounce.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(V. If any banker having the power of issue on the 6th May, 1844, should) Tj T*
(relinquish such issue, the issue department may be authorised to) Tj T*
(increase its issue of notes against securities to the extent of) Tj T*
(two-thirds of the issue so relinquished; but all the profits on such) Tj T*
(increased issue against securities were to belong to the Government.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VI. The bank must issue a weekly statement of the position of both its) Tj T*
(issue and banking departments, in a prescribed form.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VII. Bankers having the right to issue their own notes on the 6th May,) Tj T*
(1844, might continue such issue under certain conditions, and to an) Tj T*
(agreed amount; but no provision was made compelling such bankers to keep) Tj T*
(any reserve either in cash or securities against their issues. If any) Tj T*
(issue lapsed, from any cause, it could not be resuscitated; and no) Tj T*
(institutions could acquire the right of issue in the future.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VIII. Banks consisting of more than six partners, though within the) Tj T*
(sixty-five-mile radius of London, might draw, accept, or endorse bills) Tj T*
(of exchange not being payable to bearer on demand.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The first return issued by the bank in accordance with the regulations) Tj T*
(of the new act was that of the 7th September, 1844, and was as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
