(THE MERCHANT BANKERS AND ACCEPTING HOUSES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The most important function of the merchant bankers is not that of) Tj T*
(banking, but of accepting. Banking, in the strict sense of the term,) Tj T*
(they do not engage in--that is to say, they are not prepared to meet) Tj T*
(claims upon them by an immediate payment of cash or legal tender over) Tj T*
(the counter, but by payment of a cheque on one of the banks in the) Tj T*
(stricter sense of the term. The function of the London accepting houses,) Tj T*
(though of enormous importance, is still to a certain extent subordinate) Tj T*
(to the judgment of the English banks. They finally decide whose paper is) Tj T*
(most readily negotiable, and, in times when the credit machine is felt) Tj T*
(to be somewhat out of gear, the bankers occasionally discriminate) Tj T*
(against the paper of firms which they consider to have been giving their) Tj T*
(acceptance too freely. In this respect, as in so many others, the Bank) Tj T*
(of England remains the final arbiter, since the paper of an accepting) Tj T*
(house which is questioned by the other banks can be negotiated at the) Tj T*
(Bank of England through a discount house, and the Bank of England has) Tj T*
(before now intervened with effect when it considered that questions) Tj T*
(raised concerning certain acceptances have been without justification.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This business of acceptance is one into which the other banks have) Tj T*
(themselves recently intruded with considerable effect, accepting bills) Tj T*
(for their customers, home and foreign, for a commission; and there is a) Tj T*
(certain apparent anomaly in the position which makes them guardians of) Tj T*
(the volume of acceptance created by the private firms and acceptors) Tj T*
(themselves on a steadily increasing scale. Nevertheless, this anomaly) Tj T*
(has little or no untoward effect in practice. The bankers are naturally) Tj T*
(extremely cautious in raising any question as to the security of general) Tj T*
(credit in London, and they are in many ways closely connected with the) Tj T*
(private accepting houses, so that the system, which appears to be full) Tj T*
(of uncomfortable possibilities on paper, works easily enough in) Tj T*
(practice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Other functions of the merchant firms and accepting houses are their) Tj T*
