(THE DISCOUNT HOUSES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The great volume and diversity of the bills of exchange which come into) Tj T*
(the London market to be melted and turned into present cash before their) Tj T*
(date of maturity has caused the existence of a class of dealers in bills) Tj T*
(\(bill brokers\) who specialise in handling them and may be regarded as) Tj T*
(intermediaries between the holders of the bills--that is to say,) Tj T*
(originally, the drawers of them, or their representatives, or any one) Tj T*
(else into whose hands they may have passed them on--and the bankers, who) Tj T*
(are the ultimate buyers and hold them as investments until maturity. It) Tj T*
(is the business of the discount houses to buy these bills on a wholesale) Tj T*
(scale, using for this purpose funds largely lent them by the banks, and) Tj T*
(to meet the requirements of the bankers with regard to the date named) Tj T*
(and quality of the bill, providing them out of the store that they keep) Tj T*
(constantly replenished.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We have also seen that the discount houses fulfill a very important) Tj T*
(function by borrowing funds from the bankers at call and short notice.) Tj T*
(These funds are regarded by the bankers, and actually described in their) Tj T*
(balance sheets, as cash, cash at call, and short notice. It is a) Tj T*
(somewhat elastic extension of the term "cash" to apply it to money that) Tj T*
(is being lent to any borrower, even of the highest credit and against) Tj T*
(the most liquid possible collateral. But it is always assumed by the) Tj T*
(bankers that these funds placed in the discount market can be called in) Tj T*
(readily at any moment. That they can be called in is practically a fact;) Tj T*
(but it arises chiefly from the ability of the discount houses when) Tj T*
(pressed for repayment of these loans by the bankers to fill the gap in) Tj T*
(credit by an appeal to the Bank of England and the production of fresh) Tj T*
(cash, as it is called, by borrowing from it. The discount houses take) Tj T*
(security to the Bank of England and raise with it the right to draw) Tj T*
(cheques. These cheques they pay to their bankers, whose cash at the Bank) Tj T*
(of England, which we have already seen to be regularly used as a part) Tj T*
(of the basis of credit in England, is thus increased.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Besides the money that they habitually borrow for short periods from) Tj T*
(bankers, the discount houses also have considerable amounts placed on) Tj T*
(deposit with them by other lenders, some of which they employ,) Tj T*
(especially in times when the volume of bills is comparatively small, by) Tj T*
(loans to the Stock Exchange for financing the speculative commitments of) Tj T*
(the public, and by holding or carrying securities of a reasonably liquid) Tj T*
(character. They also take some part in the underwriting of new loans and) Tj T*
(in the general financial business of the London market.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([154]It is impossible to exaggerate the importance of the functions) Tj T*
(which the bill brokers discharge in the London money market. They are) Tj T*
(only about twenty in number, including three joint stock companies. One) Tj T*
