() Tj T*
(INTERVIEW WITH SIR GEORGE ANDERSON, GENERAL MANAGER[160]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. When was the Bank of Scotland founded?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. In 1695.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. When does your present charter expire?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. By act of Parliament the "governor and company of the Bank of) Tj T*
(Scotland" have "perpetual succession.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. How many branches have you?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. One hundred and sixty-three branches and twelve sub-branches in) Tj T*
(Scotland: also an office in London.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. How are your branches managed?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. By agents \(managers at London and Glasgow\) appointed by the) Tj T*
(directors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Do your branches have business relations with merchants, farmers, and) Tj T*
(all classes of people in their respective localities?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Yes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What is the law governing your note issues, and how are note issues) Tj T*
(limited and how secured?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The bank is authorised to issue, without holding coin against them,) Tj T*
(notes to the value of L396,852, but for any excess beyond that amount we) Tj T*
(must hold, at the head office, an equivalent value in gold coin,) Tj T*
(one-fourth of which may, however, be in silver coin.) Tj T*
