() Tj T*
(Q. How many branches have you?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. One hundred and fifty-two.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Are all your branches of the same class, or have you main and) Tj T*
(subsidiary branches?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. In some cases there are sub-branches. Some are mainly or almost) Tj T*
(entirely deposit branches; others have few deposits, but a large advance) Tj T*
(business.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Is the business conducted at your branches of the same class as at) Tj T*
(your office in London?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. No; the London office is itself a branch office and much of the) Tj T*
(ultimate settlement of balances takes place there. The conduct of the) Tj T*
(ordinary London business is on the same lines as that of any other) Tj T*
(London branch bank. No notes can be issued in London.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Do your branches have business relations with merchants, farmers, and) Tj T*
(all classes of people in their respective localities?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Yes, they have business relations with all classes of people.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What is the law governing your note issues, and how are note issues) Tj T*
(limited and how secured?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The act of Parliament of 1845 governs our note issue. There is no) Tj T*
(limit to the amount of notes that may be issued, but the bank is) Tj T*
(required to hold gold \(and silver to an extent not exceeding one-fifth) Tj T*
(of the total\) against the notes in the hands of the public on the) Tj T*
(average of each month, and that at its head office in Edinburgh--gold) Tj T*
(held at branch offices does not count--to an amount sufficient each week) Tj T*
(on Saturday to cover the notes in the hands of the public in excess of a) Tj T*
(certain amount specified, L216,451.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. To what extent are your notes legal tender in Great Britain?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Our notes are not legal tender at all.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
