() Tj T*
(Q. Have the managers of the branches full control of the business in) Tj T*
(granting discounts, etc.; if not, what discretion is usually given them?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Agents have power to grant advances, but subject to the approval of) Tj T*
(head office. In advances of considerable amount, an agent's duty is to) Tj T*
(get authority from the head office before granting it. The discretion) Tj T*
(allowed is dependent on the size of the branch and the nature of the) Tj T*
(business and the class of customer, and on the record of the agent. By) Tj T*
(our system of reports on advances \(weekly, monthly, and quarterly\) we) Tj T*
(keep in close touch with the advances and means of borrowers. The London) Tj T*
(branch is, of course, on different lines, and our manager there has) Tj T*
(greater powers than an agent at a branch in Scotland.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
