(THE BANK OF FRANCE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([165]The Bank of France was established in the year 1800, and was at) Tj T*
(first an entirely private concern, with a capital of $6,000,000. Among) Tj T*
(the first subscribers were Napoleon Bonaparte, Hortense Beauharnais, and) Tj T*
(bearers of names which are still prominent in the French banking world,) Tj T*
(such as Mallet, Hottinguer, Seillers, etc.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At that time, the privilege of issuing notes was not confined to a) Tj T*
(single bank. But in 1806 the Bank of France was placed under state) Tj T*
(control, and, by and by, the other issuing banks disappeared, by) Tj T*
(amalgamation or otherwise, and the Bank of France became, and has ever) Tj T*
(remained since, the only issuing bank in Continental France.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The present capital is $36,500,000, all paid, divided in $200 shares....) Tj T*
([Francs are given in terms of dollars.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These shares are held by the public, the average being about 5-1/2) Tj T*
(shares for each shareholder. One-third of the shares are held by persons) Tj T*
(possessing only one share. They are dealt in freely in the market, their) Tj T*
(quotation being at present about 465 per cent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The profits go to the shareholders, as in every other company. In 1912) Tj T*
(the bank earned a net profit of $8,200,000. The last yearly dividend was) Tj T*
(paid at the rate of 20.83 per cent....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The governor of the Bank of France and the two sub-governors are) Tj T*
(appointed by the State. They are assisted by fifteen regents, nominated) Tj T*
(by the meeting of the shareholders. The same meeting appoints three) Tj T*
(censors whom you would call auditors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The board, composed of the governors and regents, decides all questions) Tj T*
(concerning the rate of discount on loans, the issue of notes, etc.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Three of the regents, assisted by twelve shareholders chosen from) Tj T*
(amongst the prominent members of the commercial and industrial) Tj T*
(profession, compose the "discount committee," which meets at least three) Tj T*
(times a week and decides upon the acceptance or refusal of the bills) Tj T*
(presented for discount....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
