(rural or city property. In the case of summer resorts and certain other) Tj T*
(property liable to depreciate rapidly, for the sake of prudence we do) Tj T*
(not generally lend for more than thirty years; besides, the borrowers) Tj T*
(always have the right to repay at any time, and they often avail) Tj T*
(themselves of this right, so that the average length of our loans is) Tj T*
