(Q. We should like to know the general character of the business) Tj T*
(conducted by your institution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The mission of the Caisse des Depots et Consignations is to receive,) Tj T*
(hold, and repay all private funds intrusted to the State either) Tj T*
(voluntarily or under compulsion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. You say that you also do an insurance business. What do you mean by) Tj T*
(that?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The insurance office, managed by the Caisse, issues policies of life) Tj T*
(insurance, insurance payable after death or in case of accident, like) Tj T*
(any private insurance company. As regards accidents to employes while at) Tj T*
(work, it insures only against such accidents as cause death or permanent) Tj T*
(total or partial incapacity for work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Is this a corporation?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The Caisse des Depots et Consignations is not a corporation. It is a) Tj T*
(state organism, but, while charging the Caisse with the management of) Tj T*
(all private funds, which may be turned over to it by the State under) Tj T*
(different headings, the legislature bestows upon it full autonomy, in) Tj T*
(order to avoid even a semblance of possible confusion in the handling of) Tj T*
(private moneys with the handling of public moneys. Moreover, it has) Tj T*
(placed the Caisse under the direct supervision and the guaranty of the) Tj T*
(legislative powers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What is done with the profits realised from the business?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Profits earned by the Caisse on deposits of the savings banks are) Tj T*
(turned over to the reserve and guaranty fund of savings banks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What restrictions govern the investment of your funds?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. As long-term investments, we make loans to departments and) Tj T*
(municipalities, sometimes to the State; we take government rentes,) Tj T*
(treasury securities, guaranteed railroad bonds, etc. As short-term) Tj T*
(investments, we take treasury bonds, bonds of the Monte de Piete of) Tj T*
(Paris \(municipal pawnshop\), etc. Finally, we keep large sums in cash,) Tj T*
(either in our own vaults or to our credit in the treasury and the Bank) Tj T*
(of France, which, for that purpose, keep account currents on demand for) Tj T*
(us.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. You do not, as a rule, invest in mortgages?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. No; owing to the difficulty in disposing of such investments.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. You purchase no bills and do no commercial business whatever?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. No; that role is played by the Bank of France. Sometimes we make) Tj T*
(advances on securities, but only on treasury bonds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
