(Q. Your organisation is quite unique in the world, is it not?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. There is nothing like it in England or America, but there are similar) Tj T*
(institutions in Belgium and Italy, for instance. In France this) Tj T*
(institution is highly appreciated by the lawmakers, who steadily) Tj T*
(increase its functions, and the number of laws and regulations governing) Tj T*
(the Caisse is ever growing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. It is customary in France for savings banks to carry their reserve) Tj T*
(with this establishment?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The savings banks are bound to turn over to us all they receive from) Tj T*
(their depositors, except such sums as may be required to meet immediate) Tj T*
(demands.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Then, as a matter of fact, this is a central bank for the savings) Tj T*
(banks of France?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Precisely.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CREDIT AGRICOLE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(INTERVIEW WITH M. DECHARME, CHEF DU SERVICE DU CREDIT MUTUEL ET DE LA) Tj T*
(COOPERATION AGRICOLE AT THE MINISTERE DE L'AGRICULTURE[183]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What is the nature of the business of the Credit Agricole and when) Tj T*
(was it instituted?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The first law was in 1899. The first bank was opened in 1900. The) Tj T*
(Credit Agricole is based upon local organisations. France is divided) Tj T*
(into 86 departments, in each of which we are to have a regional bank) Tj T*
(\(_caisse regionale_\); and we hope eventually to have a local office) Tj T*
(\(_caisse locale_\) in each commune of each department. Among these 36,000) Tj T*
(communes there are many which are cities, which naturally would not have) Tj T*
(agricultural banks. There are only 2 out of the 86 departments in France) Tj T*
(which have not already established a regional bank.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Who furnishes the capital?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The basis of the system is the local office of the Credit Agricole in) Tj T*
(which each member--local farmers--has one or many shares of 20 francs,) Tj T*
(but on which he has to pay only 5 francs down. On payment of these 5) Tj T*
(francs he becomes a stockholder. When a local office has been) Tj T*
(established it turns all of its capital over to the regional office.) Tj T*
(Then comes the State which advances to the regional bank an amount four) Tj T*
(times the capital which has been subscribed by the local banks. The) Tj T*
(money given by the Government is not really given; it is lent without) Tj T*
(charge, without interest.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. For what purposes can this capital be used?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
