(A. The regional office does not lend directly to the farmers; it lends) Tj T*
(to the local office, and the local office has a board of directors which) Tj T*
(examines the demands of the various members.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Under what conditions do they make loans to farmers, and are their) Tj T*
(loans confined entirely to people engaged in agriculture?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The State loans to the regional office without interest; the regional) Tj T*
(office loans to the local office at 3 per cent.: the local office loans) Tj T*
(to the farmers at between 3-1/2 and 4 per cent.; in the northern region) Tj T*
(at 3-1/2 per cent.; in the southern at 4 per cent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Under what conditions?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The farmer who wants to borrow from the local office draws a bill) Tj T*
(upon himself, takes it to the local office, and the board of) Tj T*
(administration there considers it. If they approve it, the president) Tj T*
(signs it--and it has then two signatures--and then sends it to the) Tj T*
(regional office; if the regional office has plenty of money they will) Tj T*
(lend the money directly; if not, the president of the regional office) Tj T*
(signs it--it has then three signatures and is bankable paper--and it is) Tj T*
(taken to the Bank of France. During the crisis in the south of France) Tj T*
(last year in the wine-growing region at Montpellier, the centre, the) Tj T*
(regional office had one million capital; the Government then added 4;) Tj T*
(that made 5, but they lent at that office all together 16 millions, and) Tj T*
(the difference was obtained from the Bank of France in the way described) Tj T*
(by using paper with three signatures. Before the founding of these) Tj T*
(agricultural societies it would have been difficult for a farmer to) Tj T*
(obtain the three signatures necessary to borrow from the Bank of France,) Tj T*
(and what happened last year in the south of France could not have) Tj T*
(occurred before the organisation of the Credit Agricole. It should be) Tj T*
(added there has never been one cent lost by the Credit Agricole.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Are all loans made to members?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Yes; exclusively to members.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Who can become a member?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Farmers; agricultural workmen are excluded. We do not lend to people) Tj T*
(for nourishment to support themselves. We lend them money to increase) Tj T*
(the production of the land.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Must a man have some share in the crops?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. We lend money to buy a horse, a cow, or to buy fertilizer. We will) Tj T*
(lend to a man who rents a farm, but does not own it, to buy machinery,) Tj T*
(cattle, etc., but we will not lend to a man who wants to borrow the) Tj T*
(money for his own consumption; we do not lend money for a man to buy a) Tj T*
(coat, for instance. These local offices are in communities where) Tj T*
(everybody knows everybody else, and they always ask what the man wants) Tj T*
(to borrow for, and if he says he wants 400 francs to buy a cow, they) Tj T*
