(Another system consists in the division of work and specialisation,) Tj T*
(customary in England, but which has been frequently abandoned of late.) Tj T*
(In England the issuing and syndicate business is carried on by special) Tj T*
(houses which, like Rothschild, do not call themselves bankers, but) Tj T*
(merchants. Brokers and jobbers carry on stock broking on the stock) Tj T*
(exchange and in the open market, the former \(theoretically at least\) on) Tj T*
(account of third persons and the latter on their own account. It is the) Tj T*
(exclusive business of other firms to place credit at the disposal of) Tj T*
(home and foreign firms by giving acceptance to bills. These firms,) Tj T*
(strange to say, are mostly of German origin \(Fruehling & Goschen,) Tj T*
