(on free business practice in England without any legal compulsion.) Tj T*
(Consequently, no opposition is offered in that country to the different) Tj T*
(methods of carrying on business employed by the so-called foreign banks,) Tj T*
(_i. e._, the numerous branches of continental banks, including the) Tj T*
(branch offices of the Deutsche Bank, the Dresdner Bank, and the) Tj T*
(Disconto-Gesellschaft, despite the fact that their competition is) Tj T*
(unpleasant for the English institutions. In Germany, in consequence of) Tj T*
(business requirements and also of the small amount of capital in the) Tj T*
(country at the beginning of its modern economic development, the) Tj T*
(peculiar system has developed that credit banks combine all kinds of) Tj T*
(financial business \(generally with the sole exception of mortgage-credit) Tj T*
(transactions\), so that every customer can settle all his financial) Tj T*
(affairs in one spot on comparatively the cheapest terms possible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Account-current transactions form the fundamental branch of business.) Tj T*
(The bank undertakes all the financial business of its client in return) Tj T*
(for a moderate commission on the turnover calculated on that side of the) Tj T*
(account which happens to be the greater, makes and receives payments,) Tj T*
(collects bills, checks, and other documents, and pays, or charges,) Tj T*
