(Raiffeisen bank is never what a Schulze-Delitzsch bank sometimes is; a) Tj T*
(handsome building with barred windows, within which are a number of) Tj T*
(clerks discharging a constant round of business, while the directors) Tj T*
(interview special clients in a room apart. It is a small single room,) Tj T*
(probably at the back of a farm building, opened twice a week and) Tj T*
(presided over by a single occupant--the accountant. Business is apt to) Tj T*
(proceed desultorily; a small child brings in a few savings; an hour) Tj T*
