(open market, require a special organisation. Hence central organisations) Tj T*
(act as money equalisers between the different societies. In some) Tj T*
(districts money is superabundant, in others it is deficient. The central) Tj T*
(bank acts as a channel through which the abundance of one district can) Tj T*
(be drawn to supply the scarcity of another, the operations being) Tj T*
(conducted by means of current accounts with both parties. In Germany as) Tj T*
(a whole the societies of small agriculturists of the Southwest have) Tj T*
(always an abundance of money, which is one reason why they dispense so) Tj T*
(much of their funds in the purchase of property transfers. The societies) Tj T*
