(Q. What is the relation between this bank and other banks, such as the) Tj T*
(Deutsche and the Dresdner--that is, as to the character of business) Tj T*
(transacted? Are you not competitors?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. It may be said that the Reichsbank is more restricted by law. At a) Tj T*
(private bank the rate of discount may be much cheaper than at the) Tj T*
(Reichsbank. The private banker knows his clients, and he may be willing) Tj T*
(to accept from them a bill that the Reichsbank would not and could not) Tj T*
(accept.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Then there is to some extent competition?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Yes; but that competition is not large. It is not felt that the) Tj T*
(Reichsbank is a competitor of other banks, but it is a public) Tj T*
(institution. The Reichsbank has its official rate, which is higher than) Tj T*
(the private rate. A bank will take bills on its own account running) Tj T*
(three months or more and hold them, and in case of need will take bills) Tj T*
(running ten days or less to the Reichsbank for discount. The Reichsbank) Tj T*
(pays no interest and acts as agent for transfer of currency and credit) Tj T*
(to all parts of the Empire without charge.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Has there been any feeling that your branches were supplanting the) Tj T*
(private local banks in small towns?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. There may have been some instances where a banker may have been) Tj T*
(dissatisfied at the Reichsbank opening a branch in his locality, but as) Tj T*
(a rule the banks at such a place are quite pleased to have the) Tj T*
(Reichsbank open a branch in order that they may have the benefits of its) Tj T*
(facilities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. The government deposits are received and treated exactly the same as) Tj T*
(the deposits of farmers?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Yes. The business for the Government and its departments is handled) Tj T*
(the same as for others, and no interest is paid on deposits. There is,) Tj T*
(however, one exception; every private institution is required to keep a) Tj T*
(minimum balance to its credit, but not so with the departments of the) Tj T*
(Government. The Empire keeps in the aggregate sufficient to compensate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Do you always charge a higher rate of discount for bills when you) Tj T*
(have a large amount of taxed notes outstanding?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. No. On occasions the Reichsbank has not increased its rate of) Tj T*
(discount above 5 per cent. At times we have discounted even at 3 per) Tj T*
(cent., when we have had to pay a tax of 5 per cent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. It has been suggested to us as a matter of policy in times of stress) Tj T*
(that it would be better for you to add the 5 per cent. tax to the rate) Tj T*
(of discount.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
