(A. The Reichsbank must be considered in the first place as a public) Tj T*
(institution which has to take care of the public interest, and) Tj T*
(secondarily as a money-making institution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Is there any restriction as to the percentage of silver in your) Tj T*
(reserve?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. No; but there is another law, the coinage act, by which the amount of) Tj T*
(silver coined depends upon the population. They do not coin more than 20) Tj T*
(marks per capita.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What steps do you take to increase your gold reserve or to protect) Tj T*
(it?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. We always have a large amount of bills of exchange payable in foreign) Tj T*
(countries, payable in gold. We also increase the rate of discount. We) Tj T*
(consider that the latter measure is the only effective one. We also make) Tj T*
(advances without interest to importers for the time the gold is in) Tj T*
(transit; we do that even in times when the ordinary gold import point is) Tj T*
(not reached. Then we may raise our tariff for the purchase of foreign) Tj T*
(gold coins, as the Bank of England does.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Do you take any steps to prevent exports of gold? We have been told) Tj T*
(that it is the habit of the Reichsbank, in case of large exports of gold) Tj T*
(from Germany, to suggest to the other banks that it is not agreeable to) Tj T*
(have the gold exported.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. It has never been the case and never will be the case that any such) Tj T*
(suggestion has been made by the Reichsbank to anybody.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(KOENIGLICHE SEEHANDLUNG) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(ROYAL SEA-TRADE SOCIETY\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(INTERVIEW WITH HERR GEH. OBERFINANZRAT LOTTNER, DIRECTOR OF THE ROYAL) Tj T*
(SEEHANDLUNG, PRUSSIAN STATE BANK[192]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. When was this bank organised?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. In 1772.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What is the capital of the bank?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. One hundred million marks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
