(A. The money was originally invested by stockholders in the time of) Tj T*
(Frederick II, but afterwards the shareholders gave up their stock, for) Tj T*
(which they were paid. The shares were mostly owned by the King and by) Tj T*
(his associates, and they handed them over to the bank, so the capital is) Tj T*
(really owned by the bank itself. The proceeds in excess of all the) Tj T*
(expenses are paid to the Prussian State.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Who is responsible for the conduct of the business?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. The president.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Has he associated with him directors?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. No; he is personally responsible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. By whom is the president appointed?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. By the King of Prussia for life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What are the particular functions of the bank?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. In the first place, it is an organisation to help the State of) Tj T*
(Prussia. The principal part of the business is to finance the loans of) Tj T*
(the State. It may undertake the loans alone, but as a rule it heads a) Tj T*
(syndicate of the large banks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Do you compete for deposits from merchants, manufacturing concerns,) Tj T*
(banks, etc., with the Deutsche Bank or the Dresdner Bank?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
