(BANK DES BERLINER KASSEN-VEREINS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(INTERVIEW WITH HERR HOPPENSTEDT[195]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. When was this bank organised?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. In 1823, under the general companies act.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. What are its particular functions?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. This bank might be called strictly a clearing bank. It clears) Tj T*
(transactions made on the stock exchange and also cheques on banks which) Tj T*
(do not clear through the Reichsbank Clearing House. As you know, our) Tj T*
(banks do a large stock exchange business. It is their custom to send to) Tj T*
(us all securities sold to others clearing through us with a list of the) Tj T*
(purchasers. We charge the purchasers the amounts due from them and) Tj T*
(credit the amounts received from them, balancing every night. The) Tj T*
(securities are delivered to the various purchasers. _Some settlements) Tj T*
(are made daily and others monthly._ A large volume of cheques and bills) Tj T*
(are also cleared. This is simply a clearing business.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. You show loans and discounts in your statement. What is the character) Tj T*
(of these?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. We invest our funds in first-class loans and prime bills.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Is this bank owned by the other banks?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. It is partly owned by other banks. There is also a commission of) Tj T*
(shareholders of the bank, among whom are the first banks of our city.) Tj T*
(These are members of our board.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Q. Is it the custom for all banks which clear through you to have a) Tj T*
