(how powerful an influence on industry, trade, and investment is exerted) Tj T*
(by the centralisation and control of bank reserves. The London _Statist_) Tj T*
(has calculated the ultimate increased lending power of American banks,) Tj T*
(under the federal reserve system, at $3,000,000,000.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(EUROPEAN WAR) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Fourth. The European war has suddenly stimulated the tendencies which) Tj T*
(were previously evident. It has temporarily cut off a considerable) Tj T*
(amount of European trade in South America, thus leaving an opening for) Tj T*
(even more rapid development of our trade than would otherwise have taken) Tj T*
(place. It has deprived South America for a period of several years of) Tj T*
(the steady inflow of European capital. It has enormously increased the) Tj T*
(exports and decreased the imports of this country, thus placing suddenly) Tj T*
(at our disposal greatly enlarged financial power, possibly as much as) Tj T*
($1,000,000,000 per annum above normal. Its ultimate effect, we may) Tj T*
(safely assume, must be to increase considerably rates of interest the) Tj T*
(world over, thus stimulating the tendency toward an enlarged outflow of) Tj T*
(capital from the United States into neighbouring countries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(By reason of the war the same kind of a situation that would otherwise) Tj T*
(have developed slowly in a period of years now confronts us suddenly) Tj T*
(when we are as yet in a state of financial unpreparedness. The new) Tj T*
(machinery provided by the federal reserve act is not yet fully utilised) Tj T*
(or adjusted in its final form. It will require careful study, combined) Tj T*
(with prompt action, to utilise the financial opportunities now before us) Tj T*
(with greatest advantage to all concerned.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ENGLISH BANKS IN SOUTH AMERICA) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Although English interests have share holdings in other institutions,) Tj T*
(there are only five banks in South America that stand out as) Tj T*
(unmistakably British. In the order of their development, these are the) Tj T*
(London and River Plate, London and Brazilian, British Bank of South) Tj T*
(America, Anglo-South American Bank, and Commercial Bank of Spanish) Tj T*
(America. Each institution, with one exception, has concentrated on one) Tj T*
(country, in which it has established most of its branches and to which) Tj T*
(it has devoted its first efforts. The exception is the British Bank of) Tj T*
(South America, which has followed the contrary policy of having only a) Tj T*
(few branches strategically located in important cities; in other words,) Tj T*
(this bank has concentrated on selected cities rather than on a given) Tj T*
(territory.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ENGLISH TRADE AND BANKS DEVELOP TOGETHER) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The development of commercial banking by British interests has) Tj T*
(everywhere gone hand in hand with the development of British investment) Tj T*
(and British trade. The accounts of the railways, mercantile firms,) Tj T*
(steamship lines, public utilities, and other enterprises conducted by) Tj T*
