() Tj T*
(GERMAN BANKS IN SOUTH AMERICA) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To understand the energetic development of German banks in South America) Tj T*
(during the last forty-five years we must consider the conditions) Tj T*
(prevailing in Germany during that period and the strong forces working) Tj T*
(toward industrial and banking expansion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Beginning immediately after the Franco-Prussian War of 1870-71, German) Tj T*
(industrial interests, with the strong support of the German Government,) Tj T*
(began to struggle more vigorously and more effectively than ever before) Tj T*
(for a larger share of trade in international markets, particularly in) Tj T*
(the Far East and in South America. It was clearly realised that Germany) Tj T*
(needed a large and rapidly growing export trade in order to maintain her) Tj T*
(own prosperous development. In order to get this trade it was necessary) Tj T*
(to follow a definite programme which included the provision of better) Tj T*
(shipping facilities and of better facilities for financing. Up to that) Tj T*
(time Germany had been fully as dependent as the United States is to-day) Tj T*
(upon foreign ships and foreign banks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It was also clearly realised that the tendency was toward large scale) Tj T*
(production in most industries and that those concerns which could secure) Tj T*
(large sales in the world-wide markets would soon come to enjoy an) Tj T*
(overwhelming advantage over smaller competitors. The German industries,) Tj T*
(in conjunction with the great German banks, began to follow, therefore,) Tj T*
(a programme of concentration, which has since gone steadily forward.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These two forces--expansion in foreign markets and concentration at) Tj T*
(home--have had a controlling influence on Germany's foreign trade, and) Tj T*
(incidentally on her foreign banking.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(OTHER INFLUENCES IN BANK EXPANSION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another influence of importance is the fairly well-marked division of) Tj T*
(German industrial interests into a small number of groups, each one of) Tj T*
(which centres about and is allied to one of the great banks. To some) Tj T*
(extent this is true in other countries, especially where banking is) Tj T*
(centralised--notably in Canada, for instance--but it is especially clear) Tj T*
