(Only after the federal reserve act went into force in November, 1914,) Tj T*
(was it possible for any bank organised under the national-bank act of) Tj T*
(the United States to establish branches abroad. The act restricts this) Tj T*
(privilege to institutions having capital and surplus of $1,000,000 or) Tj T*
(more, and gives the Federal Reserve Board discretion to withhold its) Tj T*
(consent. Up to this writing the only institution which has taken) Tj T*
(advantage of the powers granted by the federal reserve act to enter) Tj T*
(South America is the National City Bank of New York, which has) Tj T*
(established branches in Buenos Aires, Montevideo, Rio de Janeiro,) Tj T*
(Santos, and Sao Paulo. Other branches will probably be established in) Tj T*
(the near future. Especial attention is being given to the collection of) Tj T*
(credit information. The bank also maintains a foreign trade department,) Tj T*
(which gives information and advice to its depositors as to building up) Tj T*
(business abroad. This department is now equipped to make specific) Tj T*
(reports on trade openings in Argentina, Uruguay, Brazil, Colombia, and) Tj T*
(Venezuela.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Buenos Aires branch, which was the one first established, is) Tj T*
(understood to have done a satisfactory amount of exchange business. It) Tj T*
(stood ninth in volume of clearings in January, 1915, among the) Tj T*
(twenty-odd commercial banks of that city. The other branches have not) Tj T*
(been in operation long enough to show clear results. The branches in) Tj T*
(Argentina \(including the subbranch at Montevideo\) and Brazil have each) Tj T*
($1,000,000 allocated to them--though this is purely formal, as the) Tj T*
(bank's whole capital and surplus are behind the obligations of every) Tj T*
(branch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The expansion of the National City Bank in South America has been much) Tj T*
(more rapid than that of any preceding institutions, including even the) Tj T*
(aggressive German banks. As a natural result, there is apparently less) Tj T*
(effort at this stage to build up local connections and influence in each) Tj T*
(city. So far the policy of the National City Bank appears to be to) Tj T*
(furnish foreign trade facilities to American exporters over as wide a) Tj T*
(territory as possible, rather than to concentrate its activities in any) Tj T*
(restricted region.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Other national banks in this country are known to be desirous of aiding) Tj T*
(in the financing of foreign trade, but have not up to this time found it) Tj T*
