(In several of the South American countries there is a well-organised) Tj T*
(system of land-mortgage banks following European models. In some cases) Tj T*
(the banks are owned and operated by the National Government and in other) Tj T*
(cases receive some special support or guarantee. The plan under which) Tj T*
(they all operate is the following: The owner of land who desires to) Tj T*
(raise money on mortgage approaches the bank and requests an) Tj T*
(investigation and appraisal, the expenses of which he usually pays. If) Tj T*
(the property is shown to be unencumbered with prior claims and meets) Tj T*
(other conditions, the bank delivers to the owner the mortgage bonds in) Tj T*
(convenient denominations up to a given proportion, usually 50 per cent.,) Tj T*
(of the appraised value. These mortgage bonds are part of a series and) Tj T*
(are themselves secured, not by any specific piece of property, but by) Tj T*
(all the property covered by the series; they are also backed by the) Tj T*
(credit of the issuing bank. The owner of the property then offers the) Tj T*
(bonds for sale through a broker, and in this way obtains the desired) Tj T*
(funds. He pays the bank a small commission, from one-fourth of 1 per) Tj T*
(cent. to 1 per cent., for its services.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
