(favour of European-owned banks to the relative disadvantage perhaps of) Tj T*
(American banks. This condition is the presence in some of the large) Tj T*
(South American cities, notably Buenos Aires, of a large colony) Tj T*
(representing each one of several important European nations. Naturally) Tj T*
(the tendency of each colony is to support banks of its own nationality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the whole, although this matter of national affiliations is) Tj T*
(undoubtedly a factor to be reckoned with, it appears to be by no means) Tj T*
(decisive. The German banks, for instance, have been able to expand with) Tj T*
(much greater rapidity than we should have been justified in expecting on) Tj T*
(the basis of their national trade and national colonies alone. This is) Tj T*
(true likewise of the Italian and French banks. A great proportion of the) Tj T*
(business men of South America, even those of foreign origin, are) Tj T*
(governed less by their national sentiments than by their business) Tj T*
(interests.) Tj T*
