(may be roughly compared to agricultural States like Iowa, Kansas, and) Tj T*
(Nebraska as they were thirty years ago. Farming methods are usually not) Tj T*
(economical. The small farmers have little money of their own, their) Tj T*
(lands are heavily mortgaged, and they are "carried" from one crop to) Tj T*
(another by the local general retailer, who makes advances to them both) Tj T*
(in goods and in money. The retailer must in turn secure liberal credits) Tj T*
(from wholesalers, who are in their turn partly "carried" by the banks.) Tj T*
(There is no clear-cut distinction between dealers in commodities and) Tj T*
(bankers, for the dealers are forced to finance most of their own sales.) Tj T*
(Such an arrangement of course favours extravagant credits, high prices,) Tj T*
(speculation, and crises, just as it did in the United States. It is) Tj T*
(rapidly giving way to a more complex organisation, in which the farmer) Tj T*
(has funds of his own, does his short-term borrowing at a bank, and pays) Tj T*
(cash for his purchases.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
