(Farmers as a rule think that rates are fixed arbitrarily by the bankers) Tj T*
(and other money lenders in the community. That fundamental laws of) Tj T*
(supply and demand have any controlling influence is apt to be) Tj T*
(overlooked. Without attempting to justify the high rates let us state) Tj T*
(some of the conditions which help to explain them. The demand for) Tj T*
(capital in a growing state is always greater than can be met by the) Tj T*
(local supply. In 1890, North Dakota farms were mortgaged for) Tj T*
($11,168,854; in 1910, for $47,841,587; in 1920 it will doubtless reach) Tj T*
($150,000,000. Outside capital is attracted into the state by high rates) Tj T*
(of interest. Two life insurance companies, the Union Central of) Tj T*
(Cincinnati and the Northwestern Mutual of Milwaukee, loan heavily in the) Tj T*
(state. In 1910 the Union Central Life Insurance Company reported a total) Tj T*
(investment of $5,489,087.33 in North Dakota real estate. Local banks use) Tj T*
(farm mortgages in borrowing money from banks in large cities outside of) Tj T*
(the state. Every town and village has its money-lender who acts as agent) Tj T*
(for foreign investors in farm mortgages. Banks within the state compete) Tj T*
(for capital by offering high rates of interest on time deposits, and pay) Tj T*
(all the way from 4-1/2 to 7 per cent. interest on deposits. The rate on) Tj T*
(loans must necessarily be higher under these circumstances than where) Tj T*
(banks are paying 2-1/2 and 3 per cent. interest. The high interest rate) Tj T*
(paid on bank deposits is evidence of the lack of local capital to) Tj T*
(satisfy the local demand.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The inability to attract foreign capital on lower terms is due primarily) Tj T*
(to the character of the investment. The newness of the state, the) Tj T*
(instability of its population, the character of its agriculture, all) Tj T*
(make for uncertainty. Hence the speculative character of the farm) Tj T*
(mortgage as security for a loan. In the eastern counties where the land) Tj T*
(has long been under cultivation, where the population is more stable,) Tj T*
(and where mixed farming has in a large measure supplanted the bonanza) Tj T*
(wheat farm, rates are correspondingly lower than in the newer portions) Tj T*
(of the state. As the element of risk is eliminated from investments,) Tj T*
(interest rates will come down. At least this seems to be the consensus) Tj T*
(of opinion among bankers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The character of the farming is frequently mentioned as a prominent) Tj T*
(factor in the credit situation. A crop failure under a single crop) Tj T*
(system, such as is practised in North Dakota, is likely to find the) Tj T*
(farmer in bad straits. The payment of interest on the mortgage is) Tj T*
(delayed or deferred. The local bank or loan company is obliged either to) Tj T*
(carry the farmer along for a year or to foreclose. Since many farm) Tj T*
