() Tj T*
(Consumers desiring a reduction in the cost of food supplies will be) Tj T*
(interested in a study of the operations of cattle loan companies and in) Tj T*
(the development which these may reasonably attain as a result of the) Tj T*
(provision in the Federal Reserve Act for the rediscounting of) Tj T*
(agricultural paper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The cattle loan company, commonly referred to as "cattle bank," is a) Tj T*
(middleman between borrowing cattle-owners and lending bank-managers. Its) Tj T*
(business methods and forms closely parallel those of real estate) Tj T*
(mortgage loan companies except for the fact that cattle loans are of) Tj T*
(shorter duration and secured by mortgages of the chattel variety. Cattle) Tj T*
(loan companies, incorporated under state charters, have been operating) Tj T*
(in such cities as Fort Worth, Denver, East St. Louis, St. Joseph,) Tj T*
(Portland, South St. Paul, Omaha \(2\), and Kansas City \(3\), some of them) Tj T*
(for over twelve years; and one is now being organized in Chicago. These) Tj T*
(companies have a paid-in capital stock ranging from $50,000 to $300,000,) Tj T*
(and are usually closely affiliated with a national or state bank, as are) Tj T*
(trust companies in the larger cities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These companies are informed of desired loans through country bankers,) Tj T*
(or by receipt of direct applications, the latter usually from the larger) Tj T*
("cattle-growers." In some cases the company on its own initiative urges) Tj T*
(cattlemen in whom it has particular confidence to undertake feeding) Tj T*
(operations at a time when the beef market offers a favorable opportunity) Tj T*
(for such production. In every case a salaried examiner of the company) Tj T*
(inspects the plant and herd of the cattle-grower and his personal) Tj T*
(capacity and integrity before the granting of a loan. And thereafter the) Tj T*
(examiner, on his regular circuit, maintains a continuous inspection and) Tj T*
(volunteers advice designed to protect the value of the security given) Tj T*
(for the loan. When a loan application has been acted upon favorably, a) Tj T*
(promissory note and chattel mortgage are taken. The funds of the company) Tj T*
(then advanced to the borrowers may be utilized to buy more cattle, to) Tj T*
(pay outstanding debts such as those for feeding expense, or, as is often) Tj T*
(the case, to buy the very cattle which are pledged as security for the) Tj T*
(loan. In a few cases where the cattle-grower enjoys an exceptional) Tj T*
(credit, funds will be advanced for the full purchase price of a herd for) Tj T*
(seasonal feeding purposes, or to develop two-year-olds into finished) Tj T*
(four-year-old beef cattle. The loans granted are seldom less than 60 per) Tj T*
(cent. of the known value of the cattle.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
