(apprehend that they shall have, a difficulty in meeting their) Tj T*
(engagements." Professor E. D. Jones says: "A crisis is the sudden) Tj T*
(application of a critical conservatism to business transactions, leading) Tj T*
(to such a demand for liquidation as to cause a widespread inability) Tj T*
(among business men to meet their obligations." Senator Theodore E.) Tj T*
(Burton states: "The word crisis, if employed with entire accuracy,) Tj T*
(describes a period of acute disturbance in the business world, the) Tj T*
(prevailing features of which are the breakdown of credit and prices and) Tj T*
(the destruction of confidence. It has especially to do with the) Tj T*
(relations of debtor and creditor.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
