(much greater change in its profits, if volume of output and expenses) Tj T*
(remain the same. Since the value of the factory as a going concern is) Tj T*
(the capitalized value of its prospective profits, a large increase of) Tj T*
(profits will cause a large increase of the factory's value, provided the) Tj T*
(high profits are expected to continue long. Hence the law that "the) Tj T*
(value of producers' goods tends to fluctuate more violently than the) Tj T*
(value of consumers' goods." It follows that:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     "A slight rise in the price of consumers' goods will so) Tj T*
(     increase the value of the producers' goods which enter into) Tj T*
(     their production as to lead to larger investments in) Tj T*
(     producers' goods. The resulting larger market for producers') Tj T*
(     goods again stimulates the production of such goods, and) Tj T*
