(of loans, and exceedingly high rates of interest--in short, the) Tj T*
(phenomena of crisis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The contraction of loans is accompanied by a reduction of deposit) Tj T*
(currency and a slower circulation both of money and of checks. Hence) Tj T*
(prices decline. Again the rate of interest follows; but just as it was) Tj T*
(slow to rise so now it is slow to fall. Then the business men who borrow) Tj T*
(find that the sluggish adjustment of interest reduces their profits.) Tj T*
(Therefore loans, and the deposits based on loans, contract again. But) Tj T*
(the shrinking volume of deposit currency causes a further fall of) Tj T*
(prices, and once more interest lags behind and renews the process. Thus) Tj T*
