(3. CRISES AND PANICS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Once begun, the process of liquidation extends rapidly, partly because) Tj T*
(most enterprises which are called upon to settle their maturing) Tj T*
(obligations in turn put similar pressure upon their own debtors, and) Tj T*
(partly because, despite all efforts to keep secret what is going) Tj T*
(forward, news presently leaks out and other creditors take alarm.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(While this financial readjustment is under way, the problem of making) Tj T*
(profits on current transactions is subordinated to the more vital) Tj T*
(problem of maintaining solvency. Business managers concentrate their) Tj T*
(energies upon providing for their outstanding liabilities and upon) Tj T*
(nursing their financial resources, instead of upon pushing their sales.) Tj T*
(In consequence, the volume of new orders falls off rapidly. That is, the) Tj T*
(factors which were already dimming the prospects of profits in certain) Tj T*
(lines of business are reinforced and extended. Even when the) Tj T*
