() Tj T*
(At the opposite extreme from crises of this mild order stand the crises) Tj T*
(which degenerate into panics. When the process of liquidation reaches a) Tj T*
(weak link in the chain of interlocking credits and the bankruptcy of) Tj T*
(some conspicuous enterprise spreads unreasoning alarm among the business) Tj T*
(public, then the banks are suddenly forced to meet a double strain--a) Tj T*
(sharp increase in the demand for loans, and a sharp increase in the) Tj T*
(demand for repayment of deposits. If the banks prove able to honor both) Tj T*
(demands without flinching, the alarm quickly subsides. But if, as has) Tj T*
(happened twice in America since 1890, many solvent business men are) Tj T*
(refused accommodation at any price, and if depositors are refused) Tj T*
(payment in full, the alarm turns into panic. A restriction of payments) Tj T*
(by the banks gives rise to a premium upon currency, to hoarding of cash,) Tj T*
(and to the use of various unlawful substitutes for money. A refusal by) Tj T*
(the banks to expand their loans, still more a policy of contraction,) Tj T*
(sends interest rates up to three or four times their usual figures, and) Tj T*
(causes forced suspensions and bankruptcies. There follow appeals to the) Tj T*
(Government for extraordinary aid, frantic efforts to import gold, the) Tj T*
(issue of clearing-house loan certificates, and an increase of bank-note) Tj T*
(circulation as rapid as the existing system permits. Collections fall) Tj T*
(into arrears, domestic-exchange rates are dislocated, workmen are) Tj T*
(discharged because employers cannot get money for pay-rolls or fear lest) Tj T*
(they cannot get pay for goods when delivered, stocks fall to extremely) Tj T*
(low levels, even the best bonds decline somewhat in price, commodity) Tj T*
(markets are disorganized by sacrifice sales, and the volume of business) Tj T*
(is violently contracted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(That crises still degenerate on occasion into panics in America, but not) Tj T*
(in England, France, or Germany, arises primarily from differences in) Tj T*
(banking organization and practice. In each of the three European) Tj T*
(countries, the banking system as a whole is so organized by the) Tj T*
(prevalence of branch banking and the existence of a central bank that) Tj T*
(reserves which bear a small proportion to the aggregate demand) Tj T*
(liabilities of all the offices can be applied when and where they are) Tj T*
(most needed. The central bank not only carries a reserve which is far in) Tj T*
(excess of immediate requirements in ordinary times, but also uses this) Tj T*
(reserve boldly in times of stress, presenting in both these respects a) Tj T*
(marked contrast to the policy of American banks. As a result, European) Tj T*
(business men need not fear either a refusal to lend or a restriction of) Tj T*
(payments by the banks on which they depend. And panic has small chance) Tj T*
(to develop where the depositor can get his money at need and the solvent) Tj T*
(business man can borrow. [Written before the establishment of the) Tj T*
(Federal Reserve system.]) Tj T*
