(4. DEPRESSION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The close of a panic is usually followed by the reopening of numerous) Tj T*
(enterprises which had been shut during the weeks of severest pressure.) Tj T*
(But this prompt revival of activity is partial and short-lived. It is) Tj T*
(based chiefly upon the finishing of orders received but not completely) Tj T*
(executed in the preceding period of prosperity, or upon the effort to) Tj T*
(work up and market large stocks of materials already on hand or) Tj T*
(contracted for. It comes to an end as this work is gradually finished,) Tj T*
(because new orders are not forthcoming in sufficient volume to keep the) Tj T*
(mills and factories busy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There follows a period during which depression spreads over the whole) Tj T*
(field of business and grows more severe. Consumers' demand declines in) Tj T*
(consequence of wholesale discharges of wage-earners, the gradual) Tj T*
(exhaustion of past savings, and the reduction of other classes of family) Tj T*
(incomes. With consumers' demand falls the business demand for raw) Tj T*
(materials, current supplies, and equipment used in making consumers') Tj T*
(goods. Still more severe is the shrinkage of investors' demand for) Tj T*
(construction work of all kinds, since few individuals or enterprises) Tj T*
(care to sink money in new business ventures so long as trade remains) Tj T*
(depressed and the price level is declining. The contraction in the) Tj T*
(physical volume of business which results from these several shrinkages) Tj T*
(in demand is cumulative, since every reduction of employment causes a) Tj T*
(reduction of consumers' demand, and every decline in consumers' demand) Tj T*
(depresses current business demand and discourages investment, thereby) Tj T*
(causing further discharges of employes and reducing consumers' demand) Tj T*
(once more.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(With the contraction in the physical volume of trade goes a fall of) Tj T*
(prices. For, when current orders are insufficient to employ the existing) Tj T*
(equipment for production, competition for what business is to be had) Tj T*
(becomes keener. This decline spreads through the regular commercial) Tj T*
(channels which connect one enterprise with another, and is cumulative,) Tj T*
(since every reduction in price facilitates, if it does not force,) Tj T*
(reductions in other prices, and the latter reductions react in their) Tj T*
(turn to cause fresh reductions at the starting point.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As the rise of prices which accompanied revival, so the fall which) Tj T*
(accompanies depression is characterized by certain regularly recurring) Tj T*
(differences in degree. Wholesale prices fall faster than retail, the) Tj T*
(prices of producers' goods faster than those of consumers' goods, and) Tj T*
(the prices of raw materials faster than those of manufactured products.) Tj T*
(The prices of raw mineral products follow a more regular course than) Tj T*
(those of raw forest, farm, or animal products. As compared with general) Tj T*
(index numbers of commodity prices at wholesale, index numbers of wages) Tj T*
(and interest on long-time loans decline in less degree, while index) Tj T*
(numbers of discount rates and of stocks decline in greater degree. The) Tj T*
(only important group of prices to rise in the face of depression is) Tj T*
(that of high-grade bonds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
