(enterprises which have actually become or which threaten to become) Tj T*
(insolvent, by the sale of other enterprises at low figures, by reduction) Tj T*
(of rentals and refunding of loans, by charging off bad debts and writing) Tj T*
(down depreciated properties, and by admitting that a recapitalization of) Tj T*
(business enterprises--corresponding to the lower prices of stocks--has) Tj T*
(been effected on the basis of lower profits.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(While these reductions in costs are still being made, the demand for) Tj T*
(goods ceases to shrink and then begins slowly to expand--a change which) Tj T*
(usually comes in the second or third year of depression. Accumulated) Tj T*
(stocks left over from prosperity are gradually exhausted, and current) Tj T*
(consumption requires current production. Clothing, furniture, machinery) Tj T*
(and other moderately durable articles which have been used as long as) Tj T*
(possible are finally discarded and replaced. Population continues to) Tj T*
(increase at a fairly uniform rate: the new mouths must be fed and the) Tj T*
(new backs clothed. New tastes appear among consumers and new methods) Tj T*
(among producers, giving rise to demand for novel products. Most) Tj T*
(important of all, the investment demand for industrial equipment) Tj T*
(revives; for though saving may slacken it does not cease, with the) Tj T*
(cessation of foreclosure sales and corporate reorganizations the) Tj T*
(opportunities to buy into old enterprises at bargain prices become) Tj T*
(fewer, capitalists become less timid as the crisis recedes into the) Tj T*
(past, the low rates of interest on long-term bonds encourage borrowing,) Tj T*
(the accumulated technical improvements of several years may be utilized,) Tj T*
(and contracts can be let on most favorable conditions as to cost and) Tj T*
(prompt execution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Once these various forces have set the physical volume of trade to) Tj T*
(expanding again, the increase proves cumulative, though for a time the) Tj T*
(pace of growth is kept slow by the continued sagging of prices. But) Tj T*
(while the latter maintains the pressure upon business men and prevents) Tj T*
(the increased volume of orders from producing a rapid rise of profits,) Tj T*
(still business prospects become gradually brighter. Old debts have been) Tj T*
(paid, accumulated stocks of commodities have been absorbed, weak) Tj T*
(enterprises have been reorganized, the banks are strong-all the clouds) Tj T*
(upon the financial horizon have disappeared. Everything is ready for a) Tj T*
(revival of activity, which will begin whenever some fortunate) Tj T*
(circumstance gives a sudden fillip to demand, or, in the absence of such) Tj T*
(an event, when the slow growth of the volume of business has filled) Tj T*
(order books and paved the way for a new rise of prices. Such is the) Tj T*
(stage of the business cycle with which the analysis began, and, having) Tj T*
