(MOORE'S "RAINFALL" THEORY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([246]To Professor Moore the fundamental problem of economic dynamics is) Tj T*
(to formulate the law governing the "ebb and flow of economic life" which) Tj T*
(is "the most general and characteristic phenomenon of a changing) Tj T*
(society." The motto of the department of agriculture of the United) Tj T*
(States--"Agriculture is the foundation of manufacture and commerce"--is) Tj T*
(significant and that the farmer is at the mercy of the weather is) Tj T*
(proverbial. There may be such a close connection between the weather,) Tj T*
(the crops, and crises that we shall be able to find in weather changes) Tj T*
(the cause of crises.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An examination of all the numerous factors involved in the problem would) Tj T*
(be a stupendous task and Professor Moore limits himself to a) Tj T*
(consideration of a selected few. "The variation in the quantity of the) Tj T*
(rainfall is one of the weather changes known to have a marked effect) Tj T*
(upon the yield of the crops." Hence the inquiry is directed to an) Tj T*
(examination of the "appropriate data with reference to three things: \(1\)) Tj T*
(the periodicity of rainfall; \(2\) the effect of rainfall on the crops;) Tj T*
(\(3\) the relation of the yield of the crops to economic cycles." The) Tj T*
(study is a statistical one conducted with the greatest of care to avoid) Tj T*
(error and the conclusions are deserving of the most careful) Tj T*
(consideration. All generalizations are made carefully and used) Tj T*
(cautiously with a full realization that a limited area--the upper) Tj T*
(Mississippi Valley--has been used and a period of only seventy-two years) Tj T*
(surveyed. Of the numerous climatic factors only rainfall has been) Tj T*
(examined.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Remembering that these limitations are fully realized we may state the) Tj T*
(conclusions in Professor Moore's own words: "The fundamental, persistent) Tj T*
(cause of the cycles in the yield of the crops is the cyclical movement) Tj T*
(in the weather conditions represented by the rhythmically changing) Tj T*
(amount of rainfall; the cyclical movement in the yield of the crops is) Tj T*
(the fundamental, persistent cause of economic cycles." This should be) Tj T*
(supplemented with a statement of the law that has been sought and which) Tj T*
(may be formulated thus:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     The weather conditions represented by the rainfall in the) Tj T*
(     central part of the United States, and probably in other) Tj T*
(     continental areas, pass through cycles of approximately) Tj T*
(     thirty-three years and eight years in duration, causing like) Tj T*
(     cycles in the yield per acre of the crops; these cycles of) Tj T*
(     crops constitute the natural, material current which drags) Tj T*
(     upon its surface the lagging, rhythmically changing values) Tj T*
(     and prices with which the economist is more immediately) Tj T*
(     concerned....) Tj T*
