(reserve equal in amount to at least 25 per cent. of its deposits,) Tj T*
(including not only individual deposits but deposits by bankers for whom) Tj T*
(it acts as reserve agent or correspondent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(~The Reasons for the System.~--This rather complicated system of reserves) Tj T*
(was authorized by Congress because it was necessary to allow the banks) Tj T*
(of the country districts or smaller cities to keep reserves in other) Tj T*
(banks in the larger centres of trade in order to facilitate the) Tj T*
(commercial exchanges of the country; and also because it was necessary) Tj T*
(to have some means by which banks of the larger cities could finance) Tj T*
(payments for their customers in the great centres of the country,) Tj T*
(especially in New York, Chicago, and St. Louis....) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(~Its Weaknesses.~--Our system of deposited reserves has failed miserably) Tj T*
(in times of stress, although it has worked reasonably well in ordinary) Tj T*
(times. It is contended that it has, to a large degree, built up the) Tj T*
(great centres, and more especially New York City, at the expense of) Tj T*
(country districts. It has been responsible for the seasonal withdrawal) Tj T*
(of money which was at one time a most serious embarrassment to business,) Tj T*
(especially in New York, Chicago, and other large cities in the fall) Tj T*
(months, but which has practically disappeared in New York City since the) Tj T*
(panic of 1907.... It was not until the system of deposited reserves) Tj T*
(brought about the panic of 1907 that the country at large became) Tj T*
(convinced that this feature of the national banking system was vicious,) Tj T*
(dangerous, and likely to produce trouble at any time. With this) Tj T*
(conviction began the movement which finally ended in the enactment of) Tj T*
(the Federal Reserve Act.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(~Much of Our Reserve Fictitious.~--As a matter of fact, the actual) Tj T*
(available reserves of the three classes of national banks in the country) Tj T*
(are much less than is indicated by the percentage specified in the act) Tj T*
