(NATIONAL BANK NOTES UNSOUND AND UNSAFE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([257]... Any correct system of credit currency must be based on a) Tj T*
(foundation of gold. Bank credit is issued in the two forms of deposits) Tj T*
(and notes. The former are based on a reserve of gold, the latter are) Tj T*
(not. We have here a fundamental weakness of our bank-note system. Under) Tj T*
(proper banking methods, deposits cannot expand without a proportional) Tj T*
(increase of the gold reserves of the banks. This furnishes the natural) Tj T*
(and necessary check to inflation. Our bank notes, however, have no such) Tj T*
(connecting link with the business and the monetary stock of the world.) Tj T*
(The basis of the American bank-note currency is the government debt, a) Tj T*
(very inferior kind of foundation. Such a system carries with it the) Tj T*
(possibility of paper money inflation of a peculiarly dangerous kind,) Tj T*
(because its real meaning is apt to be concealed. For example, between) Tj T*
(January 1, 1900, and January 1, 1908, the volume of national bank notes) Tj T*
(outstanding increased from $246,000,000 to $690,000,000, an expansion of) Tj T*
($444,000,000. In other words, the circulation nearly trebled in eight) Tj T*
(years. The cause of this great increase was not the need of more) Tj T*
(currency but the changes in the National Bank Act made in 1900, changes) Tj T*
(which made the establishment of national banks easier and the issue of) Tj T*
(notes more profitable.... The future is likely to witness further) Tj T*
(expansion, unless some change is made in our system.... It is) Tj T*
