(are valuable because they are security for national bank notes. This) Tj T*
(looks very much like lifting oneself by one's bootstraps.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If we are to cling to the bond-secured note system, this matter of the) Tj T*
(artificial value of government bonds will become an important practical) Tj T*
(problem whenever it becomes necessary for the United States to make any) Tj T*
(addition to its debt. Either the rate of interest will have to be raised) Tj T*
(to 3 per cent. or higher, or, if that alternative is rejected, means) Tj T*
(will have to be found to induce the banks to use the greater part of the) Tj T*
(new loans as security for additional note issues.[258] In practical) Tj T*
(effect, this is only a thinly disguised resort to the time-honored but) Tj T*
(now thoroughly discredited practice of compelling the people to use the) Tj T*
(government debt as a circulating medium.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The bearing of this matter on the safety of the national bank note is) Tj T*
(simple. The burden of the ultimate redemption of the bank notes has been) Tj T*
(placed on the shoulders of the Treasury, to add to its other burdens of) Tj T*
(maintaining the value of the greenbacks and of the silver dollars. If) Tj T*
(loss of confidence in the bank notes should ever lead people to demand) Tj T*
(their wholesale redemption, the Treasury would have to meet the demand) Tj T*
(in gold. But the moment it tried to sell the bonds, it would find there) Tj T*
(was no market for them except at a discount of perhaps 30 or 40 per) Tj T*
(cent. It is true that the Treasury would still be able to recoup itself) Tj T*
(for this loss in the value of the bonds by exercising its prior lien on) Tj T*
(the assets of the banks. But this leads us to the important conclusion) Tj T*
(that the final security for our bond-secured notes rests on the assets) Tj T*
(of the banks after all. A more striking argument for asset currency) Tj T*
(could hardly be discovered.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It must be remembered, however, that the foreclosure by the Government) Tj T*
(of its claim on the assets of the national banks would cut into the) Tj T*
(wealth on which deposits are based and so have a most disastrous effect) Tj T*
(on the deposit system. The pressure upon the Government to refrain from) Tj T*
(such a crushing blow to credit would be overwhelming. It is almost) Tj T*
(inconceivable that in time of panic or a national crisis the Government) Tj T*
(would resort to such a procedure. Almost any alternative would be) Tj T*
(preferred. It would not be too difficult a matter for the Government to) Tj T*
(persuade itself that the wiser and safer course would be to suspend) Tj T*
(specie payments, perhaps even declaring the bank notes a legal tender. A) Tj T*
(more plausible case could be made out in favor of such action than was) Tj T*
(found sufficient to justify the issue of the greenbacks of the Civil) Tj T*
(War. Yet such action would mean the breakdown of our financial system.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
