(course, means the real interest, or income on the investment, called) Tj T*
(basis, taking into consideration coupon interest, price paid, and date) Tj T*
(of maturity. Excepting for the tax of 1/2 per cent. on the circulation) Tj T*
(taken out \(1 per cent. if taken out on the 3's or 4's\) and for the) Tj T*
(expenses attendant on taking out circulation, which the government) Tj T*
(actuaries compute to average $63 on the $100,000, this interest on the) Tj T*
(government bonds looks like clear "velvet." It would be, too, if the) Tj T*
