(powers and resources. Good management cannot be secured with certainty) Tj T*
(by means of legislative provisions, however carefully designed with that) Tj T*
(end in view. In the particular instance of the Federal Reserve Act, an) Tj T*
(ingenious combination of government and banking influence in selecting) Tj T*
(the management is provided. Purely banking operations are very largely) Tj T*
(to be handled by boards of directors, a majority of the membership of) Tj T*
(which is to be chosen by banks. General supervision, and for some) Tj T*
(purposes control, is placed with the Federal Reserve Board, which is to) Tj T*
(be appointed by the President of the United States, by and with the) Tj T*
(advice and consent of the Senate. Experience alone can determine the) Tj T*
(wisdom of these arrangements for securing effective management.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Federal Reserve Banks are to exercise wide powers, and would seem) Tj T*
(likely to have ample resources. The country is to be divided into not) Tj T*
(less than eight, nor more than twelve districts, in each of which a) Tj T*
(federal reserve bank is to be established.[288] All national banks are) Tj T*
(required, and qualified state banking institutions are invited, to) Tj T*
(subscribe to the capital of the reserve bank in their district.) Tj T*
(Subscribing banks, to be known as member banks, are required to keep a) Tj T*
(part of their reserve with their Federal Reserve Bank. These banks will) Tj T*
(presumably receive most if not all of the general funds of the United) Tj T*
(States Government. They will provide an elastic currency, issuing notes) Tj T*
(secured by their commercial assets. They are also empowered to undertake) Tj T*
(the business of collecting, and clearing checks throughout the entire) Tj T*
(country, thus providing an organization for making settlements between) Tj T*
(banks in different places, the lack of which has been one of the most) Tj T*
(serious defects in our banking system.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Each Federal Reserve Bank will be a central bank for the section of the) Tj T*
(country which it is to serve. It will have all the responsibilities and) Tj T*
(most of the powers of central banks in the various European countries;) Tj T*
(but largely because the system is to be superimposed upon a fully) Tj T*
(developed banking system, some important provisions of the Federal) Tj T*
(Reserve Act are unlike anything to be found in European legislation. The) Tj T*
(Federal Reserve Banks are to receive deposits from the Government and) Tj T*
(from member banks only. Ordinarily they will lend to member banks only.) Tj T*
(All European central banks, though the bulk of their business is with) Tj T*
(banks and bankers, may deal with the general public and do so. The most) Tj T*
(striking divergence from European example, however, is the really novel) Tj T*
(plan of a system of regional banks in place of a single central bank.) Tj T*
(But the extent of this divergence is generally exaggerated. Political) Tj T*
(boundaries are indeed in large measure economic and financial boundaries) Tj T*
(as well; but central banks in the European countries do act and react) Tj T*
(upon each other, often working in harmony, and yet at times very much at) Tj T*
(cross purposes. If all Europe were brought under a single government,) Tj T*
(very likely the various existing central banks would be merged into a) Tj T*
(single institution. In some respects this would be advantageous, but it) Tj T*
(would not be absolutely necessary. Certainly European arrangements are) Tj T*
(not so fundamentally unlike those of a system of regional banks in a) Tj T*
(single country of great size, as to afford ground for the opinion that) Tj T*
(in setting up this system foreign experience has been altogether) Tj T*
(disregarded.) Tj T*
