(Many bankers bitterly condemned the compulsory features in the act while) Tj T*
(it was on its passage through Congress. This feeling was perfectly) Tj T*
(natural, but it was not very generally shared outside banking circles.) Tj T*
(Impartially considered, the act imposes no unreasonable burden upon) Tj T*
(those who have invested capital in national banks. No one fears the loss) Tj T*
(of the funds which may be subscribed to the capital stock of the federal) Tj T*
(reserve banks or placed on deposit with them. If loss should be) Tj T*
(incurred, it would be primarily due to unsound banking on the part of) Tj T*
(the boards of directors of the Reserve Banks, a majority of the) Tj T*
(membership of which is to be chosen by the banks themselves. Some) Tj T*
(bankers have doubted whether the act would prove an effective measure of) Tj T*
(banking reform; but few if any have felt that results under its) Tj T*
(operation could possibly be more unsatisfactory than those under the) Tj T*
(present system; and all agree that it is a long step toward a perfected) Tj T*
(system.) Tj T*
