(ORGANIZATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The new system is to be organized under the supervision and direction of) Tj T*
(the "Reserve Bank Organization Committee," consisting of the Secretary) Tj T*
(of the Treasury, the Secretary of Agriculture, and the Comptroller of) Tj T*
(the Currency. The most important function of this committee is to) Tj T*
(determine, "with due regard to the convenience and the customary course) Tj T*
(of business," the number and area of the Federal Reserve districts into) Tj T*
(which the country is to be divided, and to designate the city in each) Tj T*
(district in which a Federal Reserve Bank is to be established. Not less) Tj T*
(than eight, nor more than twelve districts are to be created. This is a) Tj T*
(most difficult task. However carefully the initial lines of demarcation) Tj T*
(may be drawn, more or less modification is to be expected after there) Tj T*
(has been some experience with the working of the system. Changes in area) Tj T*
(of districts, and additional districts if the organization committee) Tj T*
(designates less than twelve, may be made at any time in the future by) Tj T*
(the Federal Reserve Board. While the rivalry of cities may tempt the) Tj T*
(committee to start the system with a larger number, it is to be hoped) Tj T*
(that it will be found feasible to begin with no more than eight or nine) Tj T*
(districts. The problems which will confront the management of the) Tj T*
(Federal Reserve Banks are in many respects unlike those with which our) Tj T*
(bankers have had experience. A somewhat higher average of capacity in) Tj T*
(the management may more confidently be looked for if the smaller number) Tj T*
(of banks is established. Moreover, especially at the outset, mere size) Tj T*
(will contribute not a little to the prestige of the banks, and so) Tj T*
(inspire public confidence in the new system. A greater variety of) Tj T*
(occupations in large areas will lessen, though not much, extremes of) Tj T*
(seasonal variation in demands for accommodation upon the federal reserve) Tj T*
(banks. Then, too, the task of the Federal Reserve Board in supervising) Tj T*
(and co-ordinating the system will be materially simplified, if the) Tj T*
(minimum rather than the maximum number of federal districts is decided) Tj T*
(upon.) Tj T*
