(inconsistencies of grammar and syntax, was not planned by some master) Tj T*
(mind centuries ago, but is the result of countless ages of effort on the) Tj T*
(part of the human animal, guided only by his sub-conscious) Tj T*
(intelligence--that which we call instinct in the lower animals--to give) Tj T*
(expression to his emotions and his more or less hazy concepts. Language,) Tj T*
(like the comb in which the bee stores its honey, has come to us as the) Tj T*
(product of the labor of our ancestors through many millions of years.) Tj T*
(Money, credit, and banking are in like manner evolutionary products. If) Tj T*
(we attempt to tinker with them artificially without regard to the) Tj T*
(lessons of experience and in disregard of the forces of evolution,) Tj T*
