(check up many abuses and correct many evil situations which in the past) Tj T*
(have been ignored or glossed over by examiners in their hasty and) Tj T*
(incomplete investigations.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I thank you, gentlemen, for the opportunity to address you. Approaching) Tj T*
(the study of this new and revolutionary measure with the caution natural) Tj T*
(to every man trained in banking under the system with which we have) Tj T*
(grown up, I have become more thoroughly aroused to its merits and more) Tj T*
(deeply impressed as I have watched the methods of construction, the) Tj T*
(processes of growth, and have considered the underlying principles) Tj T*
(directing those who did the work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE ELASTICITY OF NOTE ISSUE UNDER THE NEW CURRENCY LAW[299]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To anyone who has been interested in currency reform for, say, twenty) Tj T*
(years, probably nothing is more striking than the change in emphasis) Tj T*
(which has taken place among the advocates of reform during this period.) Tj T*
(The typical reform plan of the earlier time, for example the so-called) Tj T*
(Baltimore plan brought forward in 1894, devoted itself almost) Tj T*
(exclusively to providing a thoroughly elastic note issue, based on) Tj T*
(ordinary assets. In contrast, the new law has as its central, primary) Tj T*
(object the organization into at least regional unity of something like) Tj T*
(the entire banking system of the country. Doubtless this difference in) Tj T*
(the two reform plans was not altogether due to a fundamental difference) Tj T*
(of opinion with respect to what would be the ideal scheme. The reformers) Tj T*
(of the earlier period were not indifferent to the need for centralized) Tj T*
(organization in the banking system. But they considered any scheme) Tj T*
(involving a central bank, like the old Bank of the United States, quite) Tj T*
(chimerical; and they were probably right. But times change; and men) Tj T*
