(From the beginnings of agitation for currency reform the advocates of) Tj T*
(elasticity have recognized more or less clearly two kinds: \(1\) what we) Tj T*
(may call _seasonal_ or ordinary elasticity, and \(2\) what we may call) Tj T*
(_emergency_ elasticity. By the former was meant the power of a note) Tj T*
(issue to adjust its volume to those moderate changes in the need for) Tj T*
(money which show themselves in the course of an ordinary year. By) Tj T*
(emergency elasticity was meant the power of a note issue to adjust its) Tj T*
(volume to those extraordinary changes in need which connect themselves) Tj T*
(with the typical banking panic. The evils which it was believed that) Tj T*
(seasonal or ordinary elasticity would remedy were principally \(1\) the) Tj T*
(summer shortage of currency for moving crops, together with the) Tj T*
(temporary but more or less serious stringency in the New York money) Tj T*
(market which accompanies that shortage, and \(2\) the plethora or excess) Tj T*
(of currency which usually appears three or four months after the) Tj T*
(crop-moving period has terminated. The evils which emergency elasticity) Tj T*
(was expected to relieve were principally \(1\) the stringency which) Tj T*
(precipitates the panic, \(2\) the money famine consequent on general bank) Tj T*
(suspension after the panic has fully developed, and \(3\) the glut of) Tj T*
(currency which attends the depression following a panic, often leading) Tj T*
(to excessive exports of gold and thus endangering the whole credit) Tj T*
(system of the country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
