(an old-fashioned advocate of elasticity is inclined to impose upon it,) Tj T*
(yet, when we take the new law as a whole, it seems not unreasonable to) Tj T*
(affirm that it promises to accomplish, directly or indirectly, most of) Tj T*
(the ends which we had hoped to attain through elasticity and hence) Tj T*
(promises to give us a system which in essentials is truly and adequately) Tj T*
(elastic.) Tj T*
