(A year's experience in the operation of the Federal Reserve Act has) Tj T*
(confirmed the Board in its profound conviction that the act has been one) Tj T*
(of the most beneficial pieces of legislation ever adopted by Congress.) Tj T*
(Not only have its fundamental principles been fully vindicated but in) Tj T*
(most details the working of the measure has been successful. The act,) Tj T*
(however, is a progressive piece of legislation and creates new) Tj T*
(conditions as the result of its own operation. Modification in its terms) Tj T*
(growing in part out of these new conditions will subsequently be) Tj T*
(required from time to time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For the present the Board presents the following suggestions for) Tj T*
(amendments to the act:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1\) In addition to powers now possessed in this connection by Federal) Tj T*
(Reserve Banks and national banks, the latter should be permitted to) Tj T*
(subscribe for and hold stock in banks organized for the special purpose) Tj T*
(of doing a banking business in foreign countries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(2\) With the approval of the Federal Reserve Board the issue of Federal) Tj T*
(Reserve notes to Federal Reserve Banks should be permitted either) Tj T*
(against the deposit of an equal amount, face value, of notes, drafts,) Tj T*
(bills of exchange, and bankers' acceptances acquired by Federal Reserve) Tj T*
(Banks under sections 13 and 14 of the Act, or of gold, or of both,) Tj T*
(provided, however, that gold so deposited with a Federal Reserve Agent) Tj T*
(shall count as part of the reserve required by the Act to be maintained) Tj T*
(by the bank against such notes outstanding.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(3\) The acceptance system, provision for which is made in foreign trade) Tj T*
(operations by the Federal Reserve Act, should be extended to the) Tj T*
(domestic trade in so far as relates to documentary acceptances secured) Tj T*
(by shipping documents or warehouse receipts, covering readily marketable) Tj T*
(commodities or against the pledge of goods actually sold.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There can be but little question of the safety of such acceptances, and) Tj T*
(their use will tend to equalize interest rates the country over and help) Tj T*
(to broaden the discount market.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(4\) Permission should be granted to national banks to establish branch) Tj T*
(offices within the city, or within the county, in which they are) Tj T*
(located.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(5\) In order to enable member banks to obtain prompt and economical) Tj T*
(accommodations for periods not to exceed fifteen days, the Federal) Tj T*
(Reserve Banks should be permitted to make advances to member banks) Tj T*
(against their promissory notes secured by such notes, drafts, bills of) Tj T*
(exchange, and bankers' acceptances as the law at present permits to be) Tj T*
(rediscounted or purchased; or against the deposit or pledge of United) Tj T*
(States Government bonds, the purchase of which is now permitted under) Tj T*
(the law.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(6\) The Board furthermore recommends that the power of national banks to) Tj T*
(make loans on farm lands as provided in section 24 be extended so as to) Tj T*
