(up" commercially and financially with the United States, and the) Tj T*
(slowness with which our recently reorganized banking system and our) Tj T*
(American discount market must grow, as regards international business,) Tj T*
(if it is to have roots that are strong and grow deep.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The United States has before it a great opportunity. Much depends upon) Tj T*
(the foresight with which Americans prepare themselves to meet the) Tj T*
(tremendous readjustments that will be demanded at the close of the war.) Tj T*
(That will be the supreme test. Now is the time to build for the future,) Tj T*
(and to avoid paying too much attention to immediate profits. New York) Tj T*
(can hardly be expected to succeed to London's position as the world's) Tj T*
