() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ACCEPTANCE BY MEMBER BANKS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(By act of Congress approved March 3, 1915, section 13 \(paragraphs 3, 4,) Tj T*
(and 5 of the Federal Reserve Act\) was amended and re-enacted so as to) Tj T*
(read as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Any federal reserve bank may discount acceptances which are based on) Tj T*
(the importation or exportation of goods and which have a maturity at) Tj T*
(time of discount of not more than three months and indorsed by at least) Tj T*
(one member bank. The amount of acceptances so discounted shall at no) Tj T*
(time exceed one-half the paid-up and unimpaired capital stock and) Tj T*
(surplus of the bank for which the rediscounts are made, except by) Tj T*
(authority of the Federal Reserve Board, under such general regulations) Tj T*
(as said board may prescribe, but not to exceed the capital stock and) Tj T*
(surplus of such bank.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The aggregate of such notes and bills bearing the signature or) Tj T*
(indorsement of any one such person, company, firm, or corporation) Tj T*
(rediscounted for any one bank shall at no time exceed 10 per centum of) Tj T*
(the unimpaired capital and surplus of said bank; but this restriction) Tj T*
(shall not apply to the discount of bills of exchange drawn in good faith) Tj T*
(against actually existing values.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Any member bank may accept drafts or bills of exchange drawn upon it and) Tj T*
(growing out of transactions involving the importation of exportation of) Tj T*
(goods having not more than six months' sight to run; but no bank shall) Tj T*
(accept such bills to an amount equal at any time in the aggregate to) Tj T*
(more than one-half of its paid-up and unimpaired capital stock and) Tj T*
(surplus, except by authority of the Federal Reserve Board, under such) Tj T*
(general regulations as said board may prescribe, but not to exceed the) Tj T*
(capital stock and surplus of such bank, and such regulations shall apply) Tj T*
(to all banks alike, regardless of the amount of capital stock and) Tj T*
(surplus.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In order to give effect to the above amendment of the law, the Federal) Tj T*
(Reserve Board issues the appended Regulation K, series of 1915, stating) Tj T*
(the conditions under which member banks may accept, up to 100 per cent.) Tj T*
(of their capital and surplus, drafts or bills of exchange growing out of) Tj T*
(transactions involving the importation or exportation of goods and) Tj T*
(having not more than six months' sight to run.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHARLES S. HAMLIN,) Tj T*
(Governor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(H. PARKER WILLIS,) Tj T*
